hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"13027","(13027) Bakkar bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz following the people. In homes, he forbids them from saffron."
"13028","(13028) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked for a man to enter ihram in Al-Masafartain."
"13029","(13029) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: If If there is something nice in the dyed garment, there is no harm in it for the person in ihram to wear it."
"13030","(13030) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, he said: I was with Ibn Umar and a man came to him. Two clothes were stained with saffron while he was in ihram. He said: Is there any harm in these two things? He said: Which of them is good? He said: No, he said: There is no problem with it."
"13031","(13031) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr. By limping, he was combed while he was in ihram, so his uncle Ishaq said to him: What is this? He said: It does not shake off, or it does not shake off."
"13032","(13032) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him."
"13033","(13033) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Fatima ibn al-Mundhir; Asmaa was wearing musaffar while she was in ihram."
"13034","(13034) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir, who said: I traveled with Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. Some of those with her were wearing musaffar."
"13035","(13035) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, that the wives and daughters of Abdullah bin Umar were They wear jewellery, and they are forbidden."
"13036","(13036) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: A woman in ihram should wear whatever She wants, except for the one that is rejected by the sparrow."
"13037","(13037) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d, he said: Aisha bin Sa’d narrated to me; Sa`d used to say to his daughters: “The clothes in which you are in ihram are the dyed ones. When you enter ihram, put them in them.” How are you?"
"13038","(13038) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The safflower is saturated with safflower. For women"
"13039","(13039) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he disliked mahrad for mahram."
"13040","(13040) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Sufyan, the client of Abdullah bin Iyas, who said: I saw The Companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, will enter ihram in two white and torn garments."
"13041","(13041) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Kathir ibn Jumhan, who said: A man came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, do you forbid people from wearing dyed clothes and wearing them? He said: Woe to you, it is only in the middle."
"13042","(13042) Muhammad bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Qais, who said: I saw on a peacock two garments torn with ocher. And it is forbidden."
"13043","(13043) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Haram bin Hisham, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz wearing two clothes torn, And it is forbidden."
"13044","(13044) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, who said: There was a group of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. They begin with Medina and say: We will make a pilgrimage from where the family of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, resided."
"13045","(13045) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: So you performed Hajj and have never performed Hajj. So start with Mecca, then pass through Medina if you wish."
"13046","(13046) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you want to perform Hajj and Umrah, then begin In Mecca, and make everything follow it."
"13047","(13047) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; He liked to start with Mecca, and he said: I like for my expenses to be directed to Mecca."
"13048","(13048) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: We were in Mecca and we wanted to go to Medina, so we mentioned This is from Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: One circumambulation of this House is more beloved to me than coming to Medina eight times."
"13049","(13049) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawair, on the authority of his father, he said: I went out with Alqamah. And Al-Aswad, and Amr bin Maimun, so they started in Medina before Mecca."
"13050","(13050) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God gave guidance. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He passed a sheep to the House and tied it to it. (Bukhari 1701, Muslim 958)"
"13051","(13051) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, and Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is like him. (Bukhari 1703 and Abu Dawud 1752)"
"13052","(13052) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Sheep do not imitate, nor do they sense."
"13053","(13053) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He I saw sheep being brought in imitation."
"13054","(13054) Waki` told us, on the authority of Bassam, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I saw rams imitated."
"13055","(13055) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Ata’; Aisha used to imitate sheep."
"13056","(13056) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Hamid al-Tawil, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Ubaid ibn Umair. Al-Laythi; The sheep used to be imitated."
"13057","(13057) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Salih bin Farwa, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Do not imitate the sheep."
"13058","(13058) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Ata, who said: I saw some of the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. They drive imitation sheep."
"13059","(13059) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If she enters a mahram As a janaba, let him pour water pouring over his head and do not disturb him."
"13060","(13060) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Ata’ in Ihram, when he took a bath, he said: He drank water on his head. And he does not guide you."
"13061","(13061) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in the pilgrim in ihram washing his head, and he disliked it being rubbed on his head."
"13062","(13062) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to pour water on his head without scratching it, just wiping his hand over it."
"13063","(13063) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, who said: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr pouring water on his head. Water is forbidden, and it cannot be scratched."
"13064","(13064) Hafs bin Ghayath and Abbad bin Al-Awwam narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, He said: A woman in ihram gathers her hair into three parts, and she takes a third of it."
"13065","(13065) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: A woman in ihram gathers her hair, Then you take from it as much as an fingertip."
"13066","(13066) Abbad told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, he said: I asked Ata’ about a woman’s shortening her hair? He said: You take something from its sides, but it is analysis."
"13067","(13067) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsah Ibn Sirin; Regarding a woman cutting her hair, she said: I am amazed that a young woman does not grow long, but as for the one who has passed away If she wants, she can take more, but if she does, she can take no more than a quarter."
"13068","(13068) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In a state of ihram, how do you shorten your hair? He said: Take it from the forelock."
"13069","(13069) Abu Khaled Abdul Aziz told us, he said: Shuabi told us, he said: I asked the arbiter how much should a woman cut? He said: There is nothing temporary about it."
"13070","(13070) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She cuts both her short and long hair."
"13071","(13071) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uqba, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked about the woman, how much of her hair should she shorten? He said: Like this, and placed his thumb on the second joint."
"13072","(13072) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Uqba bin Abi Salih, he said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about him? He said: Women know best."
"13073","(13073) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman should shorten her hair to the extent of her fingertip."
"13074","(13074) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, he said: I asked him: Is shaving for women better, or Negligence? He said: No, rather negligence, shortening the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"13075","(13075) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman should take her hair; Short and long."
"13076","(13076) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The one in ihram is treated. With any medicine he wants, except a medicine in which it is good."
"13077","(13077) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the hands of a person in ihram are cracked, Or his feet, let him grease them with oil, or with ghee."
"13078","(13078) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The person in ihram is treated with what He eats it"
"13079","(13079) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Khaythami, who said: I saw the black man licking his leg. With fat, which is forbidden."
"13080","(13080) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The person in ihram is treated with what He eats it"
"13081","(13081) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, who said: It was narrated to me by someone who heard Abu Dharr say: There is no harm. The pilgrim in ihram must seek medical treatment with what he eats."
"13082","(13082) Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abi Al-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Mara bin Khalid, on the authority of Abu Dharr, in a similar manner. From the hadith of Masar."
"13083","(13083) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos; They did not see any harm in a pilgrim in ihram treating his discord with ghee and oil, and Mujahid said: If you treat it with one Some of them have blood on them."
"13084","(13084) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughith al-Bajlili, who said: A discord has befallen me while I am in ihram, so I asked Abu Jafar? He said: Apply to her what you were eating."
"13085","(13085) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: The person in ihram anoints his discord with what He eats it"
"13086","(13086) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in fat for a person in ihram."
"13087","(13087) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Al-Nadr ibn Qays, who said: My wife had an epileptic seizure while she was in a mahram, so I asked Al-Qasim? He did not grant her permission, except with regard to the oil that was poured on her head."
"13088","(13088) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: There is no harm in oil for a person in ihram."
"13089","(13089) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, Amir, and Ata’, who said: There is no harm in seeking medical treatment. The person in ihram wears the mirdasang, as long as there is no perfume in it."
"13090","(13090) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I wrote to Nafi’ asking him about a person in ihram seeking medical treatment. ? So he wrote to me: Yes, it is a medicine that is not good in it."
"13091","(13091) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If the fingernail of a muhrim is broken, he should throw it away, and there is no problem. To make bitterness upon him."
"13092","(13092) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The person in ihram may seek treatment with what he likes, unless There is something good about his medicines."
"13093","(13093) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan (H) and on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of His father; They did not see any harm in a pilgrim in ihram treating his wounds with ghee and oil."
"13094","(13094) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He disliked that the pilgrim in ihram treat his hand with fat."
"13095","(13095) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A pilgrim in ihram should not be treated except with medicines that do not contain them. Good"
"13096","(13096) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, Amr ibn Aws informed him, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him to bring Aisha back, so he would grant her a lifetime of comfort. (Bukhari 1784, Muslim 135)"
"13097","(13097) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who wants to perform the Umrah from Mecca, where should he perform his ihram? He said: From Tan'im, and from it the family of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"13098","(13098) Abdou narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; Aisha was in Mecca, so when she wanted to perform Umrah, she went out to Al-Juhfah and entered ihram there."
"13099","(13099) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar and Ibn al-Zubayr left Mecca until they came to Dhul-Halif. They entered into ihram but did not enter Medina."
"13100","(13100) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman, on the authority of Salama bin Kulayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ibn Udhain, On the authority of his father; That a man came to Omar and asked him about Omar? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I did not come to you until I had ridden on camels, horses, and ships, so where did I get my people from? He said: Come to Ali and ask him. So he came to Ali and asked him? He said: From where you started, so he returned to him and told him, and he said: I do not find for you anything except what Ali said."
"13101","(13101) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ibn Udhaynah, he said: Omar was asked About Umrah while he was in Mecca, where should I perform Umrah? He said: Come to Ali bin Abi Talib and ask him. He said: So I came to him, and he said: Since the beginning, meaning from the appointed time on earth. He said: Then Omar came and informed him, and he said: I do not find for you anything except what Ali bin Abi Talib said."
"13102","(13102) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Harith Al-Taymi, he said: I had fun and met Ibn Abbas, so I said: I had fun while I was I want to perform the Ihram for Hajj, so where can I perform the Hajj? He said: From wherever you want. I said: From the mosque? He said: From the mosque."
"13103","(13103) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’n, he said: I said to Jabir bin Zayd while I was in Mecca: Where should I enter ihram from? He said: If you wish, from behind the shrine, and if you wish, from your side."
"13104","(13104) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Hisham; Al-Qasim and Salim were in Mecca and wanted to perform Umrah, so they went out to the city of Dhul-Halif."
"13105","(13105) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hammam, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about a man who came to Mecca for Umrah, then wanted to perform Hajj. On the authority of his mother? He said: He will leave at his appointed time, and Ata’ said: He will enter ihram from Mecca."
"13106","(13106) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, who said: I was living in Mecca, so I asked Mujahid: From where? Was I forbidden? He said: From wherever you wish. I said: From Dhat Irq, so that is our limit? He said: If you are in Mecca, enter ihram from wherever you wish, and if you come from another country, do not exceed the limit until you enter ihram, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, has entered ihram from the scarab, and he is coming from the sect."
"13107","(13107) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Muslim al-Qurari, who said: I said to Ibn Abbas: My mother performed Hajj but did not perform Umrah, so who Where should I perform Umrah on her behalf? He said: From your face from which you came."
"13108","(13108) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, I heard him say: {And complete the Hajj And the life is for Allah. A man asked him: What is the completion of the life? He said: To perform Umrah from where you started."
"13109","(13109) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, that she was asked: Should women have sand? She said: Are we not equal? There is no sand in the House, nor between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"13110","(13110) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Women are not required to have a guardian in the house. Nor between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah."
"13111","(13111) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no sand on women."
"13112","(13112) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Women are not required to have sand in the House, nor between the two rows. And the marwa."
"13113","(13113) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’, who said: There is no sand on women, nor between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa."
"13114","(13114) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Women tell the story, women are not required to shave, nor Sand"
"13115","(13115) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, who said: Jabir bin Zaid informed me, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married while he was in ihram. (Bukhari 5114, Muslim 47)"
"13116","(13116) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, married Maymoonah while he is in Muharram. (Bukhari 1837. An-Nasa’i 3201)"
"13117","(13117) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; He did not see any harm in marrying a mahram."
"13118","(13118) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to marry."
"13119","(13119) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: No. It is okay for a person in ihram to marry."
"13120","(13120) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a forbidden person getting married? They said: There is no harm in it."
"13121","(13121) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He gets married, I see nothing wrong with it."
"13122","(13122) Aidh bin Habib and Abd al-Wahhab bin Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, and Ali bin Hakim, On the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no harm in it."
"13123","(13123) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no problem. With it"
"13124","(13124) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Shabak, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married while he was in ihram."
"13125","(13125) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nabiyah ibn Wahb; That Omar bin Ubaid Allah bin Muammar wanted to get married while he was in ihram, so he sent to Aban bin Othman to ask him? Aban said: Othman narrated that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A person in ihram may neither marry nor engage in marriage. (Muslim 1031. Abu Dawud 1837)"
"13126","(13126) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zayd, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Rabi’a, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, On the authority of Abu Rafi’, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, married Maimun while it was permissible, and I was the messenger between them.\n(Tirmidhi 841, Ibn Hibban 4130)"
"13127","(13127) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a marriage and it was lawful."
"13128","(13128) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: Abu Fazara narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam He said: Maymunah told us; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, married her while it was lawful. (Muslim 481, Tirmidhi 845)"
"13129","(13129) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, that Omar and Ali said: A person in ihram may not marry, nor He is married, and if he is married, his marriage is invalid."
"13130","(13130) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, that Omar and Ibn Omar, one of them said: He should not marry. He does not propose, and the other said: He does not get married."
"13131","(13131) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He does not marry A person in ihram, but he should not marry."
"13132","(13132) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, who said: Zayd bin Abd al-Malik wrote to the people of Medina asks them about a woman in ihram getting married? He said: He will separate them."
"13133","(13133) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Qadamah ibn Musa, who said: My family married me to me while I was in a state of ihram, so they sent for Sa`id ibn Al-Musayyab, and he said: A person in ihram cannot marry or be given in marriage."
"13134","(13134) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’ al-Khurasani, who said: I said to Sa’id bin al-Musayyab: Ikrimah says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, got married while he was in ihram, and he said: He lied."
"13135","(13135) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The person in ihram may neither marry nor be given in marriage."
"13136","(13136) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The one who performs tamattu’ does not fast except on the tenth day."
"13137","(13137) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The one who performs tamattu’ may fast, if he wishes, a day of Shawwal, or if he wanted a day of Dhul-Qa’di. He said: Tawoos and Ata’ said: The one who performs tamattu’ does not fast except on the ten days."
"13138","(13138) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: The one who performs tamattu’ does not fast. Unless he is in ihram, nothing can be done for him except that. I said: Should he fast it from Shawwal? He said: No, except in a state of ihram."
"13139","(13139) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, and Ata’, who said: He does not fast the three days except on the tenth, and he said: Mujahid: There is no harm in fasting during the months of Hajj."
"13140","(13140) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If he fears that he will not complete the fast. In Mecca, he fasted a day or two on the way."
"13141","(13141) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say regarding someone who is on the road: If Fearing that he would not come until the day of Arafah, he fasted for three days on the way."
"13142","(13142) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If the person performing tamattu’ does not fast, he should do so. The Hadith"
"13143","(13143) Hafs and Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, who said: If he missed the fast, he should do it. The Hadith"
"13144","(13144) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; A man came to Umar performing tamattu, having missed the ten days of fasting, and he said to him: Slay a sheep. He said: I do not have it. He said: Ask your people. He said: There is no one of my people here. He said: Give him, O Mu’aqib, the price of a tea."
"13145","(13145) Hafs and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar, In a similar way"
"13146","(13146) Hafs and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There must be blood. Even if he sells his clothes."
"13147","(13147) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hikam, he said: It is necessary to shed blood, even if it is given in charity."
"13148","(13148) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: It is necessary to shed blood, even if He sells his clothes."
"13149","(13149) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If he misses the fast on the tenth day, he will break the fast. On the night of Measles, he fasted for three days, and for seven days when he returned."
"13150","(13150) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Whoever misses three days of Hajj, Let him fast on the days of Tashreeq, for they are part of Hajj."
"13151","(13151) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, or `Umar, on the authority of Aisha, who said: She used to make a concession The one who is performing tamattu may fast on the days of Tashreeq, if he does not fast the ten days."
"13152","(13152) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: If the one who is in tamattu' misses the ten days of fasting, he feeds on the three days and fasts the seven days when he returns."
"13153","(13153) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, who said: I heard him narrating on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha (h) and Salem, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: It was not permitted during the days of the Tashreeq to fast, except for those who did not He finds the guidance."
"13154","(13154) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: {And seven when you return} He said: If he wishes, he may fast on the way, and if He wanted to be in Mecca."
"13155","(13155) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding fasting for seven days, he said: If he wishes, he may fast on the way, and if he wishes, he may fast when he returns to his family."
"13156","(۱۳۱۵۶) حدَّثَنَا ابْنُ فُضَیْلٍ ، عَنْ لَیْثٍ ، عَنْ مُجَاہِدٍ ، قَالَ : صُمِ السَّبْعَۃَ إِنْ شِئْتَ فِی الطَّرِیقِ ، وَإِنْ شِئْتَ إذَا"
"13157","(13157) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he wishes, he may fast on the way, and if he wishes when he returns."
"13158","(۱۳۱۵۸) حدَّثَنَا وَکِیعٌ ، عَنْ إبْرَاہِیمَ بْنِ مَرْثَدٍ ، عَنِ ابْنِ أَبِی نَجِیحٍ ، عَنْ طَاوُوس ؛ {And seven when you return} He said: If he wishes, he can disperse."
"13159","(13159) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever performs Umrah in Shawwal Or in Dhul-Qa’dah, then he stays until he performs Hajj, then he will perform Hajj. Fasting for three days during Hajj, and seven days when he returns to his family."
"13160","(13160) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He used to see Ali The one who enjoys his body; A camel or cow, if he does not find any, he must fast for three days, and seven days if he returns."
"13161","(13161) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever performs Umrah in the months of Hajj, then he returns, but he is not able to perform Hajj. That is he who performs Hajj and does not return."
"13162","(13162) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; Like him"
"13163","(13163) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said: If he performs Umrah during the months of Hajj, then If he stays, then he is performing tamattu’, but if he returns, then he is not performing tamattu’."
"13164","(13164) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawus, and Mujahid. They said: If he goes out during the months of Hajj and then performs the So he is enjoying it."
"13165","(13165) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever performs Umrah during the months of Hajj, then returns to His country, then he performed Hajj from his year, so he is not a tamattu’. Rather, a tamattu’ is one who stays and does not return."
"13166","(13166) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Abraham, he said: I said: Those who perform Umrah in Rajab and then They stay until they perform Hajj. Will you enjoy them? He said: No, but the one who performs tamattu’ is the one who performs the Umrah during the months of Hajj, then stays until he performs Hajj. Or fasting if that is not possible."
"13167","(13167) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he performs Umrah during the months of Hajj and then stays, then he is performing tamattu."
"13168","(13168) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Like him"
"13169","(13169) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; Like him"
"13170","(13170) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: If he stays, he will have to sacrifice himself."
"13171","(13171) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The companions of If the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah during the months of Hajj, and then did not perform Hajj during that year, they were not converted."
"13172","(13172) Ibn Mubarak told us, on the authority of Saif bin Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Yazid al-Faqir; That a group of people from Kufa enjoyed their rituals and then went out to Medina and went there for Hajj, so they asked Ibn Abbas? He said: You will enjoy it."
"13173","(13173) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Whether the guided one rose or did not rise."
"13174","(13174) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever performs Umrah during the months of Hajj, then performs Hajj in its year, then he has completed Hajj."
"13175","(13175) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of the Mother of the Believers (H) and on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of The Mother of the Believers said: O Messenger of God, people begin with two rituals, and should I perform one ritual? He said: Wait, and when you are pure, go out to Al-Tan’im and be rewarded with it. Then we were thrown at such-and-such, but we According to the amount of your burden, or he said: your expenses, or as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. (Muslim 867. Ahmad 6/43)"
"13176","(13176) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Hisham Al-Mu’aiti, who said: I asked Umm Al-Darda’ about Al-Umrah after Hajj? So you commanded me to do it."
"13177","(13177) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir; He was asked about the Umrah after the days of Tashreeq? He did not see any harm in it, and said: There is no guidance in it."
"13178","(13178) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar was asked about the Umrah after Hajj? He said: It is better than nothing. And Aisha was asked? She said: According to the amount of expenses and hardship. Ali was asked? He said: It is better than an atom’s weight."
"13179","(13179) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Aisha was You perform Umrah at the end of Dhul-Hijjah."
"13180","(13180) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the Umrah after Hajj six days after the Hajj. Days? He said: Perform Umrah if you wish."
"13181","(13181) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ja’far bin Najih, who said: A man asked a peacock, He said: I was in a hurry for two days, should I perform Umrah? He said: Yes."
"13182","(13182) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Yafour, he said: We asked Ibn Umar about the Umrah after Hajj? He said: There are people who do that, and it is more beloved to me to perform Umrah on a day other than Dhul-Hijjj than to perform Umrah during Dhul-Hijjj."
"13183","(13183) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: There is no life but life. You started it from your family, and there is no life except after the beginning.\nSaeed bin Jubayr said: If he returns to his family’s place of miqat and performs Umrah, I hope it will be Umrah."
"13184","(13184) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They disliked the Umrah after Hajj, and they said: It is not sufficient, and it is not sufficient, and they said: Circumambulating the Kaaba and praying is better."
"13185","(13185) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham; That Abu Maqil came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, Umm Maqil made it obligatory for her to perform Hajj, but she did not He made it easy for her, so he said: She performs Umrah during Ramadan. (Nasa’i 4328)"
"13186","(13186) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Issa ibn Maqil ibn Abi Maqil al-Asadi, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of his grandmother Umm Maqil; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Perform Umrah during Ramadan, for it is Hajj. (Abu Dawud 1982, Darami 1860)"
"13187","(13187) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Abdullah ibn Salam, he heard a man from the Ansar He says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him and his wife: Perform Umrah during Ramadan, for your life is for both of you in Ramadan. It is equivalent to Hajj. (Ahmad 4/35)"
"13188","(13188) Waki’ told us, and Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bayan, and Jabir, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, on the authority of Wahhab bin Khanbash said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A lifetime in Ramadan is equivalent to a Hajj. (Ahmad 1771, Ibn Majah 2991)"
"13189","(13189) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: “Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj.” (Bukhari 1782, Muslim 917)"
"13190","(13190) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked him, I said: This is the greater Hajj, so what is the lesser Hajj? He said: A life in Ramadan."
"13191","(13191) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Khathim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr and Mujahid, who said: They were He performs Umrah during the month of Ramadan from the scarab."
"13192","(13192) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulaiman: He said: Ata’ and I went out during Ramadan, so we entered into ihram. From the scarab."
"13193","(13193) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham said: Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman would not perform Umrah except in Ramadan."
"13194","(13194) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Qays ibn Muslim, on the authority of Tariq ibn Shihab, he said: Abdullah was asked about Umrah during the months of Hajj? Abdullah said: (Hajj is a well-known month) but there is no Umrah in it."
"13195","(13195) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Alqamah was asked about Umrah during the months of Hajj? He said: Would anyone do that?"
"13196","(13196) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, who said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: Omar forbade the Umrah in What are the months of Hajj? Then he hesitated and said: Othman forbade it."
"13197","(13197) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Umar said: Separate your Hajj. And your Umrah, perform the Hajj in the months of Hajj, and perform the Umrah in the months other than the Hajj months, the most complete of your Hajj and your Umrah."
"13198","(13198) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I do not know that they differ that the age of Other months of Hajj are better."
"13199","(13199) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Qasim was asked about the Umrah during the months of Hajj? He said: They did not see it as complete."
"13200","(13200) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of Maimun; He said: I performed Umrah from this country of mine during other months of Hajj."
"13201","(13201) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, he said: I heard him say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah for three years, all in Dhul-Qa’dah."
"13202","(13202) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’n, who said: I saw Jabir bin Zaid and Aba Al-Aliya performing Umrah in The tithe"
"13203","(13203) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of his brother, he said: Imran bin Husayn said to me; Know that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, led a group of his family on the tenth of Dhul-Hijjah, but he did not forbid it. On his authority, but a copy of it was not revealed. Anyone said whatever they wanted about that. (Muslim 1651, Ibn Majah 2978)"
"13204","(13204) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not perform Umrah. He did not perform Umrah except during Dhul-Qa’dah."
"13205","(13205) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sadiqa ibn Yasar, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: The Umrah is in the ten days. I love it more than the Umrah after Hajj."
"13206","(13206) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the House and prayed in Mecca at noon, meaning the Day of Sacrifice. (Muslim 1100, Abu Dawud 1900)"
"13207","(13207) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Bura, who said: If the lion stoned the Jamarat on the Day of Sacrifice, he would visit home for the rest of his day, then he returns to his home for that day, until he departs with the people when they depart."
"13208","(13208) Azhar al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad preferred to come to the House on the Day of Sacrifice. Before the afternoon prayer, he circumambulates it."
"13209","(13209) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, who said: I spent the night with Sa’id bin Jubayr on the evening of The slaughter"
"13210","(13210) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to slaughter his animal behind the camel, then shave its head, then go to the House as he was, before To return to his family."
"13211","(13211) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Amr bin Amr Abi Al-Za’ara’, he said: I traveled with Abu Al-Ahwas, When it was the Day of Sacrifice, he stoned the Jamarat, shaved his head, and went to the House, but did not offer a sacrifice."
"13212","(13212) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, who said: When the lions came from Mina, they would shoot and shave, then visit House, and he does not offer a sacrifice."
"13213","(13213) I narrated on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, and Jabir bin Zaid; They visited the House on the Day of Sacrifice."
"13214","(13214) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, and Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, visited the House at night. (Abu Dawud 1993. Ahmad 1/288)"
"13215","(13215) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Dawud bin Shabur narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, he said: It was not Fayd. Of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, except for those among them who had a woman with him."
"13216","(13216) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delayed the visit until night."
"13217","(13217) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of his father: He said: We were with Abu Ayyub as a group of the Ansar, but none of us visited. He entered the house until the other party was in it, except for a man whose family was with him and he hurried with them."
"13218","(13218) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in delaying the visit until the day of departure."
"13219","(13219) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, who said: I saw al-Qasim ibn Muhammad in Minna, clothed and clothed. And he would not leave until he left on the last days of Tashreeq."
"13220","(13220) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He would not come to Mecca except when he had finished."
"13221","(13221) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ali; He used to come one day after the sacrifice, and it was said to him: He is sleeping, and he did not visit the Ka’bah after that."
"13222","(13222) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in delaying it until tomorrow."
"13223","(13223) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sa’d, who said: I met Abu Ja’far on the morning of the Day of Sacrifice, and I said: I did not I will visit the house again, and he said: I only visited today."
"13224","(13224) Ibn Uyaynah told us, saying: I heard Amr bin Dinar say a few days later: I have not visited after you."
"13225","(13225) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: I did not understand Abu Yafaid except At night"
"13226","(13226) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in him visiting the House at night. Day of Sacrifice, but not overnight in Mecca."
"13227","(13227) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he leaves him until that period passes, These days, he shed blood."
"13228","(13228) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There is no harm in delaying the visit to Day of Sacrifice."
"13229","(13229) Yahya bin Saeed and Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Hajjaj bin Abi Uthman, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj bin Amr Al-Ansari, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: Whoever performs Hajj and is broken, or lame, it is permissible for him to perform Hajj. I mentioned that to Abu Hurairah and Ibn Abbas, and they said: He has spoken the truth.\n(Tirmidhi 940, Abu Dawud 1857)"
"13230","(13230) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: God Almighty commanded retaliation. Will he accept aggression from you? Hajj for Hajj, and a life for a life."
"13231","(13231) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If a man performs the Ihram for Hajj So he is confined, then let him send his gift, and if he passes, he will make it a lifetime, and he must perform the Hajj from before, and no gift will be required of him, even if He delayed that until he performed Hajj, for which he had to perform Hajj and Umrah, and whatever Hadi was available to him, and whoever did not find it, then fasting. Three days in Hajj?? The last day is the Day of Arafah."
"13232","(13232) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Did Saeed bin Jubayr ask me about that? So I informed him, and he said, “With his hand like this,” and he tied thirty knots. This is what Ibn Abbas said."
"13233","(13233) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, who said: I heard Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr giving a sermon, and he said: O people, by God, what is the one who enjoys the Umrah until the Hajj, as you say, but rather the one who enjoys the Umrah until the Hajj; That a man performs the ihram and is confined, either due to illness, or something that detains him until the days of Hajj are over, so he comes forward and performs them. A lifetime and he performs Hajj until the next year, and he is guided and performs Hajj."
"13234","(13234) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, and Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Hajj and Umrah are upon him."
"13235","(13235) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"13236","(13236) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He must perform Hajj."
"13237","(13237) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If it is Hajj, he must reach the House with Hajj, or Umrah, and if he has not yet performed Hajj, then he must perform Hajj."
"13238","(13238) Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: Muhammad used to say: If a man assumed the intention of performing Hajj and he was struck by siesta, He will send his gift, and when the gift reaches its destination, it is permissible for some things and forbidden for others. If the coming year comes, He performs the Hajj and the Umrah, and if he combines both, he must perform the sacrifice, and if he wishes, he performs the Hajj and Umrah until he is cured, then proceeds from He faces him and circumambulates the Kaaba, performing the Umrah on his way, and he must perform the Hajj from before."
"13239","(13239) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I asked Al-Qasim and Salim about Al-Muhsaar? They said: As Muhammad said."
"13240","(13240) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Yasar; That Ma`bad ibn Hizbaba al-Makhzoumi was struck on the road to Mecca, so his son went out to the water on which his father had fallen, and found Ibn Abbas, Ibn Omar, and Marwan bin Al-Hakam, all of them mentioned the death of his father and what befell him, and all of them said: He treats himself with what is right for him. If he is right, he performs Umrah, and the prohibition of Hajj is canceled for him. If he performs Hajj, he must perform Hajj, and what Get away from the guidance."
"13241","(13241) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd, he said: We left We lived until we were near the cracks, and a friend of ours was stung, so we crossed the road, asking what we should do with him? Then Ibn Masoud was riding, so we said: Was a companion of ours bitten? So he said: Make a day of peace between you and your companion, and let him send the sacrificial animal. If the sacrificial animal is slaughtered, then it is permissible. May the Umrah be upon him."
"13242","(13242) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakhir, who said: I went out for Umrah, and when I was with some On the way, I fell off my mount and broke my leg, so I sent to Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar someone to ask them, and they said: There is no time for Umrah like the time for Hajj. It is not permissible until one circumambulates the Kaaba. So I stayed there for fifty-five months. Or eight months."
"13243","(13243) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus; Concerning a person in ihram at his age, he was interrupted, and he said: He will send a sacrificial animal, then he will calculate how much he will travel, then he will take a few days to be on the safe side. Then it is permissible."
"13244","(13244) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Yazid bin Jabir, who said: I asked Mujahid about the occurrence of a mahram. His wife? He said: This was during the reign of Omar bin Al-Khattab, so he said: They will complete their Hajj, and God knows best their Hajj, then they will return. It is permissible for each one of them to be permissible for its companion. If there is a person coming, he performs Hajj and makes sacrifices, and they disperse from the place where they arrived."
"13245","(13245) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Wahban, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to Ibn Abbas and said: I had intercourse with my wife while I was in ihram, so he said: God knows best about your Hajj. Go ahead, and you both must perform Hajj from the beginning. When you reach the place where you fell, separate, then do not Come together until you complete your Hajj."
"13246","(13246) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: Each one of them has to perform the Hajj, so when they perform Hajj from They soon dispersed from the place where they had arrived."
"13247","(13247) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Saeed bin Khurshid told me; That a man asked Jabir bin Zayd and Al-Hasan bin Muhammad for a fatwa about a man and his wife who were permitted to perform Hajj, then they agreed to it, and they said: They will complete their Hajj, and it is their duty to perform Hajj from before, and if they are able to afford it, he will present a mountain."
"13248","(13248) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, on the authority of his father, who said: A man came to Abd God bin Amr asked him about a mahram who had sexual intercourse with his wife? So he pointed to Abdullah bin Omar, but the man did not recognize him. Shuaib said: So I went with him, so he asked him? He said: His Hajj is invalidated. He said: So he should sit? He said: No, rather he goes out with the people and does what they do. When someone meets him, he performs Hajj and gives gifts. So they return to Abdullah bin Amr told him, so he sent us to Ibn Abbas. Shuaib said: So I went to Ibn Abbas with him, and he asked him? So he said to him: Like what Ibn Omar said. So he returned to him and told him, and the man said to him: What do you say? He said: Like what they said."
"13249","(13249) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: They go on. They will face each other, complete their Hajj, and return to where they liked. If he is there, they will be welcome from where they were. Because of their Hajj, which they spoiled and guided, and they separated."
"13250","(13250) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ataa, who said: They should complete their Hajj, and each one should do it. Some of them are blooded, and if it is one, then both of them are sufficient, and they must perform Hajj from the beginning, and they should not be separated."
"13251","13251) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not know how to differentiate between a man when he had intercourse while he was in ihram."
"13252","((13252) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: They have decided to perform ritual sacrifice, and upon them is a guide. Hadi, and two pilgrims from Qabil, so when they come to the place where it happened, they do not meet until they are permitted."
"13253","(13253) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubair bin Adiy, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: On each one of them. Body"
"13254","(13254) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: The fire of every one From the blood"
"13255","(13255) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata`, who said: Between them he revealed it, and Sufyan said: Tea. Partition"
"13256","(13256) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A sacrifice is due on each of them."
"13257","(13257) Ibn Numair narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Each one of them has to do as he sees fit."
"13258","(13258) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: He is a guided person from the two worlds."
"13259","(13259) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, who said: Each one of them has a burden on him."
"13260","(13260) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’, who said: Each one of them shall shed blood, if he One is their two parts."
"13261","(13261) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, who said: There is a guidance upon them both, a guidance in it."
"13262","(13262) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: They will be deprived of the place they established. Therein"
"13263","(13263) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid and Ataa, who said: They are deprived of the place in which they entered ihram."
"13264","(13264) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: If he is willing Welcome from where they were, welcome to their Hajj, which they spoiled."
"13265","(13265) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, who said: Mujahid and Sa’id bin Jubayr were sent to A giving person asks about food for ihram that contains saffron? He thought, so they said: Was he influenced by someone? He said: No, so they ate without paying attention to what he said."
"13266","(13266) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Khasif, who said: I asked Mujahid and Ata’ about the khaskanang and the yellow khabees? He thought about it and said: So I asked Saeed bin Jubayr, and he said: Do you apply oil while you are in ihram? He said: I said: No. He said: Do you apply ghee while you are in ihram? I said: No. He said: The khashkanang was cooked with fire."
"13267","(13267) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: No. There is nothing wrong with a covered Khashkanang for a person in ihram."
"13268","13268) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in the yellow khabees or the yellow khashkanang, if the fire touched him."
"13269","(13269) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Tawoos and Atta; They did not see anything wrong with the yellow khabees for the Muhrim, and they used to say: Whatever the fire touches, there is no harm in it."
"13270","(13270) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: There is no harm for a person in ihram to eat food that contains saffron."
"13271","(13271) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He did not see anything wrong with the yellow khabees and the yellow khashkanang for a person in ihram."
"13272","(13272) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: It was mentioned to Abraham that Al-Mughirah disliked eating. The yellow khashkanang in ihram, and Ibrahim used to marvel at it."
"13273","(13273) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He used to eat the yellow khashakanang while he was in ihram. He said: Abu Ja`far did not see anything wrong with food containing saffron."
"13274","(13274) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Badhimah, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubair; He hated it, then he saw no harm in it."
"13275","(13275) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He saw nothing wrong with the yellow khaskanang for the Muhrim."
"13276","(13276) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He hated it"
"13277","(13277) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father; Like him"
"13278","(13278) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Muslim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al Qasim, on the authority of his father; He disliked saffron on food for a person in ihram."
"13279","(13279) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, on the authority of Ibrahim; They did not see any harm in a person in ihram eating salt that contains saffron."
"13280","(13280) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is nothing wrong with yellow salt for a person in ihram."
"13281","(13281) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, and Tawoos; They used to hate the yellow salt of ihram."
"13282","(13282) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, who said: I asked Ja’far about yellow salt for those in ihram? His thoughts"
"13283","(13283) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, he said: I was with Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and a man said to him: I want to I entered ihram and had a garment dyed with saffron, so I washed it until the color of the saffron disappeared. Sa`id said: Do you have another garment? He said: No, he said: So enter into ihram therein."
"13284","(13284) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: He washes it and enters ihram. Therein"
"13285","(13285) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Salih bin Jubayr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, he said: I came to him. In a quilt dyed with saffron and saturated with it, I said: Should I enter ihram in this case? He said: Wash her and enter ihram over her."
"13286","(13286) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ishaq, the servant of the family of Omar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in It is forbidden to wear clothes dyed with saffron if washed."
"13287","(13287) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm for a man to enter ihram while his garment has been dyed. With saffron, then washed, it does not wash off or remove."
"13288","(13288) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the garment dyed with roses and saffron, he said: If that part of it is washed and it is gone, he will not see it as a thing if he wears it. Muharram."
"13289","(13289) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like him"
"13290","(13290) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah, who said: Wash it and enter ihram for it."
"13291","(13291) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham; That Abdullah bin Urwa asked Urwa about a dyed garment, if it is washed until its color disappears? He forbade it."
"13292","(13292) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Aisha, who said: It is disliked for a person in ihram to wear dyed clothing. With saffron, and infused with safflower for men and women, unless it is a washing garment."
"13293","(13293) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: If the dyed garment is washed, And his smell disappeared, and he said: There is no harm in entering ihram therein."
"13294","(13294) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: I asked him about lice, I found it on My face while I am in ihram? He said: Throw it away from your face, for it has no share in it."
"13295","(13295) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: A woman came to Ibn Umar and asked him, and she said: I found a lice, so I killed it, or did I kill it? He said: What is the lice of the game?"
"13296","(13296) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, who said: A man said to Ata’: Should I cast the louse and it will crawl on me? He said: Yes, he said: So should I bury myself? He said: It is disliked for you to iron your clothes while you are in ihram. He said: I said: Do ticks and lice crawl on me? He said: Abandon what is not from you."
"13297","(13297) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzoumi was asked about Does the Muhrim see lice on his clothes? He said: He took it gently, then placed it on the ground and did not let go."
"13298","(13298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The person in ihram can remove lice from himself if he wishes."
"13299","(13299) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: A tick stuck to me while I was in ihram, so I said to Talq bin Habib? He said: Throw it away, may God keep the tick away."
"13300","(13300) Ibn Mushir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated May the peace and blessings of God be upon him at the House during the Farewell Hajj on his mount, receiving the stone in his place. (Muslim 2551, Abu Dawud 1875)"
"13301","(13301) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’i, on the authority of Ikrimah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated the Kaaba on a camel, and when he came to the Black Stone, he would point to it."
"13302","(13302) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; Umm Salamah said: O Messenger of God, I have not performed the Tawaf of Exit. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: When you perform the Tawaf of Exit. Prayer: Then go around your camel behind the people.\n(Bukhari 1619 and Abu Dawud 1877)"
"13303","(13303) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came He, peace and blessings be upon him, had complained, so he went around the House on a camel and with it a camel. Every time he passed by the stone, he would pick it up, and when he finished He performed tawaaf, then prayed two rak'ahs. (Bukhari 1412 and Abu Dawud 1872)"
"13304","(13304) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Marouf al-Makki, who said: I heard Abu Tufayl, when I was a boy, saying: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, he circumambulates the Kaaba on his camel. (Muslim 927. Abu Dawud 1874)"
"13305","(13305) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, circumambulated the Kaaba on his camel, receiving the stone in his chambers, and between Safa And Al-Marwah, so I said to Ata’: What did he mean by that? He said: Expanding upon his nation."
"13306","(13306) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: Whenever my father saw them circumambulating the Kaaba, Animals are forbidden."
"13307","(13307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, rode on his camel between Safa and Marwa."
"13308","(13308) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abu Idris, who said: I saw Aisha running between the two rows. And the narration is on a mule."
"13309","(13309) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ahwas, he said: I saw a man circumambulating between Al-Safa and Al-Marwa on a donkey."
"13310","(13310) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Saad, who said, I asked Abu Ja’far about circumambulating between Safa and Marwa? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated riding, and I circumambulated riding, so he and I circumambulated riding."
"13311","(13311) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They both hated men and women riding between Safa and Marwa, unless there was an excuse."
"13312","(13312) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Kharijiyah bin Al-Harith, he said: I saw Aarak bin Malik circling between Al-Safa And the marwa is on a donkey."
"13313","(13313) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid Al-Shaybani, who said: I saw a mujahid and a generous person seeking Between Safa and Marwa on two animals."
"13314","(13314) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, who said: Whenever my father saw them striving between the two rows, And Al-Marwa is riding high. He said: These people have been disappointed and lost."
"13315","(13315) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He disliked riding between Al-Safa and Al-Marwah except for necessity."
"13316","(13316) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ya’four, who said: A man from Khuza’a, who was the commander of Hajj in Mecca, addressed us. He said: O people, Omar was a strong man, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: O Omar, you are A severe man who harms the weak. If you circumambulate the Kaaba and see a stone empty, then approach it. Otherwise, say “Allahu Akbar” and “Allah.” Flashing (Ahmad 1/28, Bayhaqi 80)"
"13317","(13317) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you stand close to him, say “Allahu Akbar” and pray and pray. Upon the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"13318","(13318) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik circumambulating the Kaaba, until when he was close to the stone, he looked. And he turned to him and said “Allahu Akbar” like him."
"13319","(13319) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I saw a man facing the pillars with the takbeer."
"13320","(13320) Abdul bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: When my father was defeated, he would face him and say “Allahu Akbar.” He flashed."
"13321","(13321) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: I saw Sa’id bin Jubayr when he began the tawaf facing the stone. He did not touch it, but he raised his hand and said “Allahu Akbar,” so I asked Ataa? He said: “Allahu Akbar,” and do not raise your hands to say “Allahu Akbar.”"
"13322","(13322) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Burjan, who said: I saw Mujahid, when he passed by the stone, he looked at it and said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"13323","(13323) Ibn Fudayl and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father: He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to Abd al-Rahman bin Awf: What have you done? He said: I received it and left it. He said: I was right. (Hakim 307. Ibn Hibban 3823)"
"13324","(13324) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Talha ibn Yahya, on the authority of al-Qasim, who said: I saw Ibn Umar crowding on the stone until he bled. Nostril"
"13325","(13325) Ali bin Masih narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: I went around with him, but he was not He crowds over the stone."
"13326","(13326) Abu Saad Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If there is crowding on the stone, then there is no You will harm me and you will not be harmed, but stay away from it."
"13327","(13327) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar ibn Amr, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, who said: He does not crowd the stone."
"13328","(13328) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He hated for you to crowd Ali. Stone, you harm a Muslim, or he harms you."
"13329","(13329) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, Mujahid, Muhammad bin Ali, Salim, and Al-Qasim. ; They were not crowding over the stone, but they were assessing the future hour."
"13330","(13330) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaid Al-Tai, who said: I saw Al-Hasan coming to the stone and seeing a crowd, so he saw He greeted him, called, then came to the shrine and prayed two rak’ahs there."
"13331","(13331) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to greet him and not crowd him, but Ibn Umar used to do that."
"13332","(13332) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Hajjaj, and Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas say: O people, your entry into the House is not part of your Hajj in any way."
"13333","(13333) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the pilgrim, he said: If he wishes, he may enter the Ka’bah, and if he wishes, he may not enter it, and he said: If he wishes, he may enter it, then fine, but if he does not, then no. It's okay, but if you enter it, go to the middle pillar and pray there."
"13334","(13334) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Khaythama; He was asked about entering the house? He said: It does not harm you, by God, if you do not enter it."
"13335","(13335) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you wish, do not enter it."
"13336","(13336) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Whoever enters the House, enters into its good, and leaves its bad, And he left forgiven."
"13337","(13337) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: Safiyya had her period after What she did, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was informed of that, and he said: Did you imprison us? I said: She circumambulated, then she had her period after that. He said: Let her go. (Muslim 383. Abu Dawud 1996)"
"13338","(13338) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, with something similar, except that He said: No then.\n(Bukhari 1757, Muslim 384)"
"13339","(13339) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned May God bless him and grant him peace. So we said: She has menstruated. He said: Sore your throat. I don’t see her except her holding us back. She said: I said: She She has circumambulated on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: No, then, narrate it, so let it go. (Muslim 965. An-Nasa’i 4189)"
"13340","(13340) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: I asked Al-Qasim bin Muhammad about a woman who visited the House on the Day of Sacrifice. Then she had her period before leaving? He said: May God have mercy on Omar. The companions of Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: It has finished, except for Omar, for he used to say: It will be the last pledge of the House."
"13341","(13341) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I did not see Ibn Abbas Someone disagreed with him about something and he left it, until he agreed with it, so Jabir bin Abdullah disagreed with him in the matter of a woman circumambulating and then menstruating. Ibn Abbas said: She should leave, so they sent for a woman who had been afflicted with this, and she agreed with Ibn Abbas."
"13342","(13342) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, he said: I heard Al-Qasim bin Rabi’i, he said: I asked Saad Ibn Malik on the authority of a woman who menstruated after circumambulating the Kaaba on the Day of Sacrifice? He said: It is issued."
"13343","(13343) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, on the authority of his father; He used to perform the Tawaf of the Day of Sacrifice for seven days, until she performed the Tawaf of the Day of Sacrifice over the menstruating woman. Alienation"
"13344","(13344) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Hani’; That a woman circumambulated and then had her period on the Day of Sacrifice after she circumambulated, so Al-Hasan bin Ali was asked? He said: Leave."
"13345","(13345) Affan told us, he said: Abu Awani told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdullah bin Aws Al-Thaqafi said: I asked Omar bin Al-Khattab about a woman circumambulating the Kaaba and then menstruating? He said: Let her last promise be with the House. Al-Harith said: Likewise, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a fatwa, and he said: Omar: I was confused about your hand. You asked me about something that you asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as if I disagreed with him.\n(Tirmidhi 946. Abu Dawud 1997)"
"13346","(13346) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ Al-Hamdadi narrated to us, on the authority of Salih Al-Dhan, who said: Jabir bin Zaid said: Fasting and prayer It improves the body, but it does not benefit the money. Charity improves the wealth, but it does not benefit the body, and I do not know of anything better. For money and body in this sense, meaning Hajj."
"13347","(13347) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Miskin, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to see that when Hajj many times, for charity is better."
"13348","(13348) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Atiyya, who said: I asked Al-Hajjaj about a man who performed the rituals of Hajj. Should he perform Hajj? Or is he freed? He said: No, rather he will be freed."
"13349","(13349) Wahb bin Ismail Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: Some people came to him His neighbours, and he said: I have prepared to go out, and I have neighbors who are in need and needy, so what do you see for me? Should I make my honor and reward among them, or should I go ahead for Hajj? He said: By God, the reward of honesty is great, and none of those situations is equal to me."
"13350","(13350) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Nothing the people have spent is greater in reward than the blood shed today. Sacrifice, except for a needy family member who may pray for it."
"13351","(13351) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Hussein bin Ali, who said: Because I provide sustenance for my family. In Medina, one saa’ every day, or two saa’s a month, is more beloved to me than one Hajj after another Hajj."
"13352","(13352) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, he said: What people do after the obligatory prayer is more beloved to me than feeding Poor person."
"13353","(13353) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’ (h) and on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Muadh bin Sa’wah, on the authority of Sinan bin Salamah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: A voluntary sacrifice cannot be eaten from it, for if it is eaten, it will be fine. (Ahmed 7)"
"13354","(13354) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muhammad bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah, they said: : If he eats from it, he will be fined."
"13355","(13355) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar, who said: Whoever gives a sacrifice voluntarily, then his throat is spoiled. Without the sanctuary, and he did not eat from it, but if he did eat, he would have to replace it."
"13356","(13356) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, who said: He sent Abdullah with him to bring him, He said: And he ordered me, when I slaughtered it, to give a third in charity, eat a third, and send a burden to my brother’s family for a third."
"13357","(13357) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; In the body, he does not have to do anything voluntary, unless he commands a command, or eats, or feeds, then He did change."
"13358","(13358) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, who said: If you eat from the voluntary offering, you will be fined."
"13359","(13359) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, who said: I had with me a sacrifice given to the poor, so he ordered me to eat from it. And he saved."
"13360","(13360) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They did not eat of anything that they had prepared for God, then They were permitted to eat of the Hadi, the sacrificial animal, and its like."
"13361","(13361) Ismail Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawus, and Mujahid; They said: It shall not be eaten from the ransom, nor from the reward of the game."
"13362","(13362) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to say: When the body becomes damaged Or it was broken, and its owner ate from it and fed it, and he did not replace it, unless it was a vow, or the reward of a hunter."
"13363","(13363) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was not the reward of a hunt, or rituals, or A vow to the poor, for one should not eat from it."
"13364","(13364) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: He shall not eat from the reward of game."
"13365","(۱۳۳۶۵) حدَّثَنَا شَرِیکٌ ، عَنْ سَالِمٍ ، عَنْ سَعِیدِ بْنِ جُبَیْرٍ ، قَالَ : لاَ یُؤْکَلُ مِنَ النَّذْرِ ، وَلاَ مِنَ الْکَفَّارَۃِ ،"
"13366","(13366) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: It is not eaten from a vow, nor from the reward of a game. Nor of what has been appointed for the needy."
"13367","(13367) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: He does not eat from the reward of a game."
"13368","(13368) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Hassan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, brushed the animal’s hair on the right hump, and the blood dried from it. (مسلم ۲۰۵۔ ترمذی ۹۰۶)"
"13369","(13369) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, and Marwan ibn Al-Hakam; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of Al-Hudaybiyah, imitated the Hady and made it hairy. (Bukhari 1694, Ahmad 4/323)"
"13370","(13370) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid, who said: Notification is not Dutifully"
"13371","(13371) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid who said: Feel the guidance if you wish, and if Whatever you want, don't feel it."
"13372","(13372) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; He sent to her, meaning, the body? She said: If you wish, she only feels it so that it is known that it is her body."
"13373","(13373) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no guidance except what is imitated and made known."
"13374","(13374) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, and Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad that they both said: He is glorified, then he is made to feel."
"13375","(13375) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Ash’ar.\n(Bukhari 1696. Muslim 957)"
"13376","(13376) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Camels imitate and feel, and cows imitate and do not They feel, but sheep do not imitate or feel."
"13377","(13377) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Qais ibn Sa’d, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If you wish, feel the guidance, but if you wish, do not feel it."
"13378","(13378) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ata’ (h), Yusuf bin Mahak, and Mansour, on the authority of Ata’; A man closed his door to a pigeon and its two chicks, then he went to Arafat and Minna, and he came back and it had died, so he came to Ibn Umar. So he mentioned that to him, so he appointed three sheep for him, and a man judged with him."
"13379","(13379) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: We camped in a house and closed the door of the house over two pigeons. Then she died, so we asked Ata? He said: There is a sheep in it."
"13380","(13380) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Shaykh Ali."
"13381","(13381) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whoever kills one of the pigeons of Mecca will do so. What a shame"
"13382","(13382) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He has a sheep."
"13383","(13383) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Mahrez, who said: I closed my door in Mecca and then opened it, and suddenly a bird flew in. They died, so I asked Tawoos? He said: Slay two sheep."
"13384","(13384) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In the sacred bird: sheep, sheep."
"13385","(13385) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ata’; In Al-Dabasi, Al-Qamari and Al-Akhdar: Tea, tea."
"13386","(13386) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of a sheikh from the people of Mecca; That a pigeon was on the house, and it fell on Omar’s hand, and he pointed with his hand, and it flew and fell on some of the houses of the people of Mecca. Then a snake came and ate it, so Omar judged himself a sheep."
"13387","(13387) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Salih bin Al-Mahdi, that His father told him, saying: I performed Hajj with Uthman and we came to Mecca, so I made a mattress for him in a house and he lay down, then a dove came and fell into it. I put a window on his bed, so she started searching with her feet, and I was afraid that she would throw it on his bed and he would wake up, so I put it on. Then she fell into another window, and a snake came out and I killed her. When Othman woke up, I told him, and he said: Bring some sheep on your behalf. So I said: I only mentioned it for your sake. He said: And on the authority of a sheep."
"13388","(13388) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The first to ransom the sacred birds with the sheep of Uthman."
"13389","(13389) Abdi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He used to say in the bathroom of the Sacred Mosque that if he was killed in Mecca, then there is a sheep in it."
"13390","(13390) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: We asked Abraham about a man who took a chick in his hand. While he was in ihram, he wanted to return it and he died? He said: He is a guarantor."
"13391","(13391) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: (Neither sexual intercourse) nor Transgressions (and there is no argument about Hajj) He said: Disagree with your companion until you anger him."
"13392","(13392) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; {And there is no argument about the Hajj} He said: The Hajj has begun during the month of Dhul-Hijjah and no month can be forgotten, and there is no doubt about the Hajj, because the people of The pre-Islamic people used to stop and perform Hajj other than Dhul-Hijjah."
"13393","(۱۳۳۹۳) حدَّثَنَا سُفْیَانُ بْنُ عُیَیْنَۃَ ، عَنْ عَمْرٍو ، عَنْ جَابِرِ بْنِ زَیْدٍ ، قَالَ : {لاَ جِدَالَ فِی الْحَجِّ} قَالَ : لَیْسَ"
"13394","(۱۳۳۹۴) حدَّثَنَا مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ فُضَیْلٍ ، عَنْ مُغِیرَۃَ ، عَنْ إبْرَاہِیمَ ، قَالَ : الرَّفَثُ إتْیَانُ النِّسَائِ ، وَالْفُسُوقُ السِّبَابُ"
"13395","(13395) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Indecent intercourse, immorality, disobedience, and quarreling."
"13396","(13396) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nadhr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: indecency is sexual intercourse, immorality is disobedience, and hypocritical argumentation."
"13397","(13397) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Indecency is intercourse, but God A nickname"
"13398","(13398) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan, he said: obscenity is deceit, immorality is swearing, and argument is disagreement. In Hajj"
"13399","(13399) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Wahib, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba; He asked Ata’ ibn Yassar about his statement: (There should be no obscenity, no immorality, and no quarreling during Hajj)? He said: indecency, incest with women, immorality, transgression, and quarreling with insults."
"13400","(13400) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Indecency: sexual intercourse, immorality, disobedience, and quarreling. To argue with your friend until you make him angry and he makes you angry."
"13401","(13401) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid: (And there is no argument regarding Hajj) He said: The matter of Hajj has been established."
"13402","(13402) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Khalid Al-Walbi, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Amr bin Muqrin, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Cursing a believer is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief. (Tabarani 80)"
"13403","(13403) Ubaidah bin Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbiy, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Amr bin Muqrin, On the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly."
"13404","(13404) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Rafth Sexual intercourse, immorality, insults, and hypocritical arguments are to quarrel with your friend to the point of angering him."
"13405","(13405) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Rafth Intercourse, immorality, sins, and hypocritical arguments."
"13406","(13406) Shababah told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; (No sexual intercourse) He said: intercourse with women."
"13407","(13407) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Amr Al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: I heard Abdullah bin Masoud says: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Cursing a believer is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief. (Abu Ali 4970)"
"13408","(13408) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Wael, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said hello, according to the hadith of Mu`tamir. (Bukhari 48. Muslim 116)"
"13409","(13409) Muhammad bin Al-Hasan Al-Asadi told us, he said: Abu Hilal told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Cursing a believer is immorality, and fighting him is disbelief. (Nasa’i 3567. Ahmad 1/178)"
"13410","(13410) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah, on the authority of Jubair bin Mut’im, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Banu Abd Manaf, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating this House and praying. Night or day. (Tirmidhi 686. Abu Dawud 1889)"
"13411","(13411) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas circumambulating after the afternoon prayer and praying."
"13412","(13412) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar circumambulating the Kaaba after dawn, He prayed the two rak'ahs before sunrise."
"13413","(13413) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Shuabi; He saw Al-Hasan and Al-Hussein approaching Mecca, so they circumambulated the Kaaba after the afternoon prayer and prayed."
"13414","(13414) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Laith; Al-Hasan, Ata’, and Mujahid used to circumambulate the Kaaba after the afternoon prayer, and they would pray at the end of their circumambulation."
"13415","(13415) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaym bin Hayyan, who said: I asked Ikrimah bin Khaled about him? He said: No problem."
"13416","(13416) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He did not see any harm in tawaaf after dawn or after the afternoon prayer."
"13417","(13417) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Juma’, on the authority of Abu Tufayl; He used to circumambulate the Kaaba after the afternoon prayer and pray until the sun set."
"13418","(13418) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I saw Ibn Umar and Ibn Al-Zubayr walking around. At home after the dawn prayer, then they prayed two rak’ahs before sunrise."
"13419","(13419) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Tawaf and pray after the afternoon prayer. And after dawn there was no time."
"13420","(13420) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah bin Urwah bin Al-Zubair; Thabit bin Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr circumambulated the Kaaba seven days after the morning prayer, but he sat and did not pray, so his father Abd came to him. Allah bin Al-Zubair, and he said: O my son, if you are performing Tawaf, then pray, and if you have not prayed, then do not perform Tawaf."
"13421","(13421) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Taman, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babah He said: I saw Abu Al-Darda’ circumambulating after the afternoon prayer and praying two rak’ahs, and it was said to him? He said: It is not like other countries."
"13422","(13422) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah used to perform tawaf. After lunch for three weeks, then when the sun rises he prays two rak’ahs every week, and after the afternoon prayer he does that. When the sun sets, he prays two rak'ahs every week."
"13423","(13423) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I saw Sa`id bin Jubayr and Mujahid circling. At home until the sun turns yellow, and they sit down."
"13424","(13424) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: If you want to circumambulate At home after the dawn prayer, or after the afternoon prayer, perform Tawaf and delay the prayer until the sun sets or until it rises, then pray Two rak'ahs for every week."
"13425","(13425) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nasr bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his grandfather Muadh Al-Qurashi; He circumambulated the Kaaba with Muadh bin Afra after dawn and after the afternoon prayer, but he did not pray."
"13426","(13426) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Omar bin Al-Khattab did Tawaf after dawn, then He rode until he came to Dhat Tawi and descended. When the sun rose and rose, he prayed two rak'ahs, then he said: Two rak'ahs in place of two rak'ahs."
"13427","(13427) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, he said: We prayed the Fajr prayer, then we sat and waited for the circumambulation. He said: Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri circumambulated, then he sat down and did not perform the prayer."
"13428","(13428) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Perhaps I took an ant by biting your arm. My stomach, so I cut off her head and the rest of her remains in my stomach."
"13429","(13429) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Walid Al-Bajli, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; In the month of Muharram, he lost a lot of seed, he said: He gives in charity."
"13430","(13430) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: Ata was asked about a man who killed many people, not knowing what he was doing. He said: He gives many dates in charity."
"13431","(13431) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I heard a peacock and a man asked him, he said: Did I make a mistake and kill an offspring? A lot? He said: Give handfuls of wheat in charity."
"13432","(13432) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’; What about ants that Muhrim kills? He said: He eats something."
"13433","(13433) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I asked Tawoos about killing the offspring in the Sacred Mosque? He said: If he hurts you, there is no harm in it."
"13434","(13434) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I asked Al-Qasim, Mujahid, Salim, Ata’, and Tawoos about Ants, grasshoppers, and lizards? They said: If it was a mistake, then he does not owe anything, but if it was intentional, then a handful of food is required, and Amer said: It is a handful of food. Was the food wrong, or intentional?"
"13435","(13435) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Imamah, he said: I asked Ibn Umar, he said: I said: I kill Mosquitoes? He said: What's wrong with you?"
"13436","(13436) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abi Ziyad, who said: I saw Salim killing a mosquito in Mecca. So I said to him? He said: He was ordered to kill the snake and the scorpion. I said: They are enemies. He said: This is an enemy."
"13437","(13437) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in killing flies and mosquitoes."
"13438","(13438) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Marzuq, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; Concerning a person in ihram who killed a fly, he said: There is no blame on him."
"13439","(13439) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nabiha bin Wahhab, on the authority of Aban bin Othman, He told him; Othman narrated, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace; Concerning a man, if his eyes complain while he is in ihram, he bandages them with patience. (Tirmidhi 952, Abu Dawud 1834)"
"13440","(13440) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he did it."
"13441","(13441) Abd ibn Sulaiman and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Whenever his eyes complained while he was in ihram, he would drip patience into them abundantly."
"13442","(13442) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel (H) and Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi, on the authority of Shu`ba, both of them on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Alqamah, said: There is no harm in a person in ihram applying kohl with kohl."
"13443","(13443) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Shamisa Al-Azdi, who said: I entered upon Aisha while I was in ihram. And I complained to my eye, and she said: Come, I will apply kohl to you, and she has an oyster that contains patience, so I refused to do so, and I regretted it afterward. That I should not abandon her."
"13444","(13444) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hilal bin Maimun, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: There is no harm in it."
"13445","(13445) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the person in ihram complains, his eyes Let him apply kohl to them with patience and chasteness, and do not use kohl with any good kohl in it."
"13446","(13446) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Zaid, who said: A man came to Al-Hasan and said: O Abu Sa’id, why? Does the ihram wear kohl? Jabir bin Zayd was beside him and said: Al-Hasan remained silent, and Jabir said: He should apply kohl with honey, but Al-Hasan did not deny that."
"13447","(13447) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, and Abu Hashim. They said: He applies patience and aloe vera as permissible. And bitterness."
"13448","(13448) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to hate black kohl for a muhrim. He said: So I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: He smeared himself with black kohl. Red"
"13449","(13449) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ammar, who said: Saeed bin Jubayr saw a woman in ihram, who had tied a cord around his head. So he cut it off."
"13450","(13450) Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu al-Zubair, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He is not a fanatic. The person in ihram is to cover his head with a belt and no rag."
"13451","(13451) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a woman in ihram tying his head, and he said: He may tie his head if he wants."
"13452","(13452) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yassar, who said: I saw Ibn Abbas When we found him, his hair was tied with a snare, and he was in ihram."
"13453","(13453) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Khalid, he said: Abu Asmaa narrated to me My servant Abdullah bin Jaafar, he said: Al-Hussein bin Ali went out on Hajj and complained about some way, so he pointed to his head, so they said Perhaps: Al-Hussein was pointing to his head, so he ordered camels to be given as charity to the people of the water, and his throat."
"13454","(13454) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Make the ransom wherever you wish."
"13455","(13455) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Whatever blood, or charity, or the reward of a game, it should be in Mecca. And fast wherever you want."
"13456","(13456) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whatever blood there was, it was in Mecca, and whatever it was due to fasting, Or give it in charity wherever you want."
"13457","(13457) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: Every bloodshed is obligatory, so he has no one to slaughter it except In Mecca"
"13458","(13458) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Mu`ashar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Whatever recompense is in Mecca, and almsgiving and fasting wherever you wish."
"13459","(13459) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, and Ash’ath, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Blood in Mecca."
"13460","(13460) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: If a woman in ihram is forced to She is a mahram, so she has to wear two camels. My body on his behalf and his body on her behalf, and if she obeys him, then each one of them must do his own and the Hajj is from before."
"13461","(13461) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’ that they said regarding Muharram: If he is forced to do so by his wife. Atonement for her. If she obeys him, then each one of them must do it as an atonement."
"13462","(13462) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; In a woman in ihram, her husband is forced to perform Hajj until he has intercourse. He said: He will perform Hajj for her with his money."
"13463","(13463) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Humaid, who said: I asked al-Sa’ib: What did you hear while living in Mecca? ? He said: I heard Al-Ala' bin Al-Hadrami saying: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Three for the immigrants after Al-Sadr. (Muslim 444. Ahmad 52)"
"13464","(13464) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, who said: I heard Amir saying: He did not befriend anyone from The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Amer used to say: What are neighbours?"
"13465","(13465) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, who said: I stayed with Jabir bin Abdullah in Mecca for six days. More months"
"13466","(13466) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, who said: Jabir bin Abdullah, Ibn Umar, and Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurairah, and Abu Saeed Al-Khudri."
"13467","(13467) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: He used to reside in Mecca. The two years"
"13468","(13468) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Abdul Malik, who said: I entered Mecca, and then Ali bin Al-Hussein and Sa’id bin A mighty one."
"13469","(13469) Ubad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I and Ubad bin Umair Al-Laythi came. Aisha was a neighbor to Thabeer. He said: She had vowed to be a neighbor for a month. He said: Abd al-Rahman was her brother. He prevented her from doing that and said: Being close to the House and circumambulating it is dearer to me and better. He said: When Abdul Rahman died, I went out."
"13470","(13470) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Omar Ibn Abi Ma’ruf, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: Omar said: Do not stay after the group except Three."
"13471","(13471) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, who said: When Ash-Sha’bi was asked about neighbourhood, he would bring the letter of the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him to Khuza’a: Indeed, I have taken for those of you who emigrated just as I have taken for myself, even if he were in his land. Not a resident of Mecca, except a Hajj or Umrah performer. (Ibn Saad 272)"
"13472","(13472) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Mecca is neither a place of residence nor a place of abode."
"13473","(13473) Ali bin Musahir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Amir, who said: It is not appropriate for a migrant to be a neighbor for more than three people. Days in Mecca"
"13474","(13474) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Khasif, who said: I took from the drink of Muhammad bin Marwan while I was in ihram, so I asked Saeed Ibn Jubayr? So he ordered me to give a dirham in charity."
"13475","(13475) Jarir told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of a Mujahid in a forbidden matter who trimmed a mustache permissibly? He said: He gives a dirham in charity."
"13476","(13476) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan hated to take the forbidden item from the head. Halal means from his hair or his pen."
"13477","(13477) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, he said: Tell me who saw some Our companions say it is forbidden to fall short of Jabir ibn Zayd and it is permissible for him to do so."
"13478","(13478) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: A woman in ihram combs her hair. Halal, you only kill the lice of others."
"13479","(13479) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of his master Al-Sa’ib bin Abdullah, she said: Al-Sa’ib ibn Abdullah used to order me to drink from the Abbas family’s water supply, and he said: It is a complete part of the Hajj."
"13480","(13480) Abbad ibn al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Drink from the Abbas family’s watering cans, and he drank from them. Muslims, and it is Sunnah."
"13481","(13481) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He said to me, “A servant of the Banu Abdullah.” Ibn Al-Sa'ib: Drink from the watering can of the family of Abbas, and the Muslims have drunk from it."
"13482","(13482) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sa’d, who said: I saw Abu Ja’far circumambulating the Kaaba, then he came. Zamzam, and he brought half of the wine from the drinker, and he drank half, and gave half to Ja`far."
"13483","(13483) Muhammad bin Abi Adi narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah Al-Muzani, who said: A man would like to He drinks from the wine of the drinker."
"13484","(13484) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abi Ismail, who said: Sa`id ibn Jubayr left Minna with Jahir. So he circumambulated the Kaaba for a week and prayed two rak’ahs, then the butler came and Muhammad bin Ali made us drink wine, and Saeed drank from it. Ibn Jubayr and Saqani."
"13485","(13485) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abdul A’la, on the authority of Suwayd bin He ignored him and said: Drink from the wine from the drinker."
"13486","(13486) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I drank some of the wine from the drinker with him. A wine from which I was struck."
"13487","(13487) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I did not see Ibn Umar in what he was doing. He never drinks wine overflowing."
"13488","(13488) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr; He performed Hajj countless times with Salim, but he did not see him drinking any of the wine from the water bottle."
"13489","(13489) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the Banu Abd al-Muttalib while they were marching against Zamzam, and he said: Dismiss the Banu Abd al-Muttalib. Al-Muttalib: If the people had not prevailed upon you to give you water to drink, I would have gone with you. So they handed him a bucket and he drank from it."
"13490","(13490) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khuthaym, who said: I spoke with Saeed bin Jubayr, and he came. A basin containing Zamzam water, so he scooped it with his hand and drank from it."
"13491","(13491) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They used to like it when they said goodbye to the House. To go to Zamzam and drink from it."
"13492","(13492) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: A man likes to drink, and to draw water from Zamzam if he can."
"13493","(13493) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: I did not see Abdullah bin Omar among those who were He continues to drink Zamzam from a cat."
"13494","(13494) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr; He did not see Salem drinking Zamzam water."
"13495","(13495) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He performed Umrah in the year of fighting, in Shawwal and Rajab."
"13496","(13496) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: Aisha was She performs Umrah at the end of Dhul-Hijjah, and performs Umrah in Medina in Rajab, and performs Ihram during Dhul-Halif."
"13497","(13497) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, who said: The black man used to perform Umrah in Rajab and then return."
"13498","(13498) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I heard Yahya Ibn Abd al-Rahman narrates, on the authority of his father; He performed Umrah with Uthman in Rajab."
"13499","(13499) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Harith, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq being asked about the age of Ramadan? He said: I realized that the companions of Abdullah do not treat the Umrah of Rajab equally, and then they begin the Hajj."
"13500","(13500) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: Al-Qasim used to perform Umrah in Rajab."
"13501","(13501) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Yahya bin Abdul Rahman bin Hatib, on the authority of his father, said: I performed Umrah with Omar and Uthman in Rajab."
"13502","(13502) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, he said: Ammar bin Ruzaq told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, she said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered the night of the group from the Batha’i.\n(Ibn Majah 3068. Ahmad 6/78)"
"13503","(13503) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, who said: I heard Sulayman bin Yassar say: Abba Rafi’ was on the weight of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I came and hit his dome with the hammer, so he came and descended.\n(Muslim 342. Abu Dawud 2002)"
"13504","(13504) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slept in the deepest sleep, then went to bed."
"13505","(13505) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Al-Ma’roor bin Suwayd, who said: Omar said: O the family of Khuzaymah, Prepare for the night of departure."
"13506","(13506) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Amr bin Murah narrated to us, he said: Al-Aswad was revealed with Al-Abtaha. He said: He heard foaming. He said: So he looked at what it was? Then he was Ibn Omar, and he was traveling."
"13507","(13507) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid, who said: I came with Sa’id bin Jubayr, and when we dispersed, we came to Al-Abtah. When We accepted from Mina."
"13508","(13508) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he reaches Al-Albah, let him put down his mount, then To visit the House and lie there for a while, then to leave."
"13509","(13509) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus; That his father used to count in the people of Al-Khuz."
"13510","(13510) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Abu Bakr and Omar used to count the numbers. (Muslim 951, Tirmidhi 921)"
"13511","(13511) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Hasib is not of anything. It is only a revelation revealed by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Bukhari 1766, Muslim 952)"
"13512","(13512) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He did not recite Al-Abtah, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, only did it because he waited for Aisha. (Ahmad 1/351)"
"13513","(13513) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God only revealed May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. Al-Abtah because he was allowed to go out, and he is not of your age. (Bukhari 1765. Abu Dawud 2001)"
"13514","(13514) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and the like."
"13515","(13515) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith; Verily, Ata’, Tawus, Mujahid, and Sa’id bin Jubayr were countless."
"13516","(13516) Abdou bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of Fatima; Indeed, the names were innumerable."
"13517","(13517) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The measles are only in the heavens."
"13518","(13518) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid; He denied it."
"13519","(13519) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; That his father did not count."
"13520","(13520) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to Al-Safa from the gate of Banu Makhzum."
"13521","(13521) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Bakr, who said: When Ibn Umar came, he circumambulated the Kaaba and prayed. He performed two rak'ahs, then he left for Al-Safa through the gate next to Al-Saqiyya."
"13522","(13522) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He did not see any harm in any of the doors of the mosque. He went out to Safa."
"13523","(13523) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: When you pray, go out through whichever gate you wish, meaning to Safa."
"13524","(13524) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: If you circumambulate the Kaaba and do not realize Whether you have completed it or not, then complete what you are in doubt, for God does not punish the extra."
"13525","(13525) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a man doubts about tawaf and does not know whether Did he turn it off, or did he not turn it off? Let him receive."
"13526","(13526) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I stoned the Jamarat, but I did not know how many I threw? So I asked Ibn Umar and he did not answer me, so Ibn al-Hanafi passed by me and I asked him? He said: O Abdullah, there is nothing greater for us than prayer, and if one of us forgets, he repeats it, so I informed Ibn Omar, and he said: They are an understanding family."
"13527","(13527) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {Then a recompense like the camels he killed} until his statement: {or the equivalent of that is fasting} He said: If a muhrim kills game, he will be judged against it. With his portion of blessings, if he cannot find it, he looks at its price, then evaluates its price as food, then fasts a day in place of every half a saa’. {Or as an expiation by feeding the poor, or is that equivalent to fasting?} He said: What is meant by food is fasting. If he finds food, he finds food. His reward"
"13528","(13528) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the Almighty’s saying: (And whoever of you kills him intentionally, his recompense will be the same as the camels he killed. Those of justice among you will judge for them. (A gift that reaches the Kaab) and if he does not find it, people will provide him with food, then it will be said to him: Fast for every day half a saa’."
"13529","(13529) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, Mujahid, and Ibrahim; They said: If a pilgrim in ihram catches the game, he must pay its price and buy blood. If he does not find any blood, he makes food and gives alms on all of it. A poor person is given half a saa’, but if he does not find that, he should fast for two days for each saa’."
"13530","(13530) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, who said: Maymun ibn Mihran mentioned the killing of a hunting man. And it was Muharram. He said: {A recompense of cattle like what he killed. Just people among you will judge it as a guide that will reach the Kaaba} if he finds it. A man gives the reward of the game as a gift, and if he does not find it, then he pays its price, then he gives it as food to give in charity to the poor. It is not possible for a person to fast one day without the food of every poor person."
"13531","(13531) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqisim, who said: He will value dirhams on him, then he will value the dirhams. food, then fast one day for every half a saa’."
"13532","(13532) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: These verses were revealed: {Not There is a burden upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord. He said: During the seasons of Hajj."
"13533","(13533) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas (h) and on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abi Yazid, On the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr; (There is no blame on you if you seek bounty from your Lord) He said: During the seasons of Hajj."
"13534","(13534) Gandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Umaymah; He asked Ibn Umar about the man performing Hajj and carrying merchandise with him? Ibn Umar said: There is no harm in it, and he recited these verses: {They seek bounty from their Lord and satisfaction}"
"13535","(13535) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw no harm in a man performing Hajj with his merchants. He said: And Muhammad said: Indeed, God is able to bring them together for Him. All of you"
"13536","(13536) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They were not trading until the verse “It is not upon you” was revealed. It is a sin that you should seek bounty from your Lord}"
"13537","(13537) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: {There is no sin upon you if You seek bounty from your Lord.} He said: They did not buy nor sell during days of deprivation, so God Almighty revealed: {Not There is a burden upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord}"
"13538","(13538) Shababih told us, on the authority of Warqa’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; (There is no blame upon you if you seek bounty from your Lord.) Commerce during the seasons was lawful to them; they used not to trade during the seasons. The pre-Islamic era of Arafah, and not from Him."
"13539","(13539) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard a man He said: Labyk on the authority of Shubrumah, and he said: If you have performed Hajj, then turn on the authority of Shubrumah, otherwise, then turn on your own behalf. (Daraqutni 156)"
"13540","(13540) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, similarly. (Abu Dawud 1807, Ibn Majah 2903)"
"13541","(13541) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab; Ibn Abbas heard a man say: Labbaika on the authority of Shubrumhi. He said: Woe to you, and what is Shubrumhi? Then he mentioned a man who was related to him and said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He said: No, he said: So keep this on your own."
"13542","(13542) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Humaid bin Al-Aswad informed us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father; Ali did not see any harm in performing the Hajj on behalf of a man."
"13543","(13543) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man performing Hajj on behalf of another man, and there has never been a Hajj? He said: It is sufficient on his behalf and on behalf of his first companion. Abu Bakr said: The one who has never performed Hajj."
"13544","(13544) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see any harm in performing Hajj on behalf of a man."
"13545","(13545) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Indeed, God is sufficient for all of them."
"13546","(13546) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; Concerning a man who is in ihram for Hajj and Umrah, and his wife is in ihram for Hajj and Umrah, so he has intercourse with her. He said: They go on. For their Hajj and for their Umrah, and each one of them will shed a blood, and their Umrah is upon them, and the Hajj is from before, and they will not pass. In the place where they struck what they struck."
"13547","(13547) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the one who falls in love with his family and he has declared the marriage with them, he said: He has two sins upon him."
"13548","(13548) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The qarin and the non-qarin are equal in the penalty of hunting."
"13549","(13549) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about a person in ihram standing, then coming back? He said: There is only one Hadi on him."
"13550","(13550) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Regarding a Muharram who repeatedly cheated on his wife, he said: If he did that before he had forgotten you and knew what was wrong with him, then he must sacrifice a sacrifice. One"
"13551","(13551) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about fasting on the Day of Resurrection. Did he know? He said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not fast, I performed Hajj with Abu Bakr and he did not fast, and I performed Hajj with Omar. He did not fast on it, and I performed Hajj with Uthman but he did not fast on it, and I do not fast on it, nor do I order it, nor forbid it.\n(Tirmidhi 751, Ibn Hibban 3604)"
"13552","(13552) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God called May God’s prayers and peace be upon him with milk on the day he found out about Umm al-Fadl’s departure, so he drank from it while he was in the situation."
"13553","(13553) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, drank on the day of Arafat. (Abu Ali 6697. Tabarani 18)"
"13554","(13554) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God broke his fast. May God bless him and grant him peace at Arafat, and Umm al-Fadl sent him some milk and he drank it. (Tirmidhi 750, Nasa’i 2820)"
"13555","(13555) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I do not know whether I heard it from Sa`id ibn Jubayr, or whether it was narrated from him. He said: I came to Ibn Abbas with Arafah while he was eating pomegranates, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, broke his fast with Arafat. Umm al-Fadl gave him milk to drink, and he drank it and said: May God curse so-and-so. They went to the days of Hajj and erased his adornment, and he said: The Hajj has become beautiful. Talbiyah\n(Nasa’i 2815. Ahmad 1/349)"
"13556","(13556) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hawshab bin Aqeel, he said: Mahdi Al-Abdi told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: I went to Abu Hurairah in his house and asked him about fasting on the day of Arafat? Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade fasting on the day of Arafat. (Abu Dawud 2432. Ahmad 2/304)"
"13557","(13557) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said May the peace and blessings of God be upon him: The Day of Arafah, the Day of Sacrifice, and some days of Mina, days of eating and drinking."
"13558","(13558) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab about fasting. The day of Arafah? He said: Abdullah bin Omar did not fast."
"13559","(13559) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sharik, on the authority of Sulaiman al-Ahwal, who said: I mentioned to Tawus a fast that he knew was Is it equivalent to fasting for two years? He said: Where were Abu Bakr and Omar about that?"
"13560","(13560) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr; He broke his fast on the day of Arafat, and said: I will strengthen myself in supplication."
"13561","(13561) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, who said: I saw Omar drinking one day He knew"
"13562","(13562) Yahya bin Muhammad bin Al-Bayhi told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I saw Ibn Umar and Ibn Al-Zubayr. They consult medicine on the eve of Arafat, and drink from it."
"13563","(13563) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated fasting on the day of Arafah if he was in Mecca."
"13564","(13564) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair; His father, Ubaid bin Umair, ordered him to break the fast on the day of Arafah."
"13565","(13565) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Amara bin Zazan, who said: I asked Salim about fasting on the day of Arafah? He said: Neither Omar nor anyone from Omar’s family fasted, my son."
"13566","13566) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha; She was fasting on the day of Arafat."
"13567","(13567) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father; He used to fast in Arafah."
"13568","(13568) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha; She used to call for a drink, break her fast, and then break the fast."
"13569","(13569) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to break his fast before he broke his fast."
"13570","(13570) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr; If he wanted to pour it over, he would call for a vessel, then drink, then pour it over."
"13571","(13571) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Aisha did not vomit until He whitens the earth between us and the people."
"13572","(13572) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: A person should stand on the eve of Arafah after Should the imam push until the crowd of people goes away? He said: There is no harm in it."
"13573","(13573) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who stood with the imam: Should he imprison his mount while the imam has departed until the crowd has gone? He said: There is no harm in it."
"13574","(13574) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to Jamarat al-Aqaba and threw it at it, but he did not stop there. (Ahmad 2/190)"
"13575","(13575) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that he used to throw stones at The two Jamarat prayers and he should stop at them, but he should not stop at the third jamarat."
"13576","(13576) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Harun bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Adiy bin Adiyy, On the authority of Salman bin Rabi’a, he said: We looked at Omar and he came to the third Jamarat and threw it at it, but he did not stop there."
"13577","(13577) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Mujahid bin Rashid, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; He did not stop there."
"13578","(13578) Ali bin Musir, Ibn Fudayl, and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, On the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas, on the authority of his mother, she said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, coming on the Day of Sacrifice. He stoned the coals of Al-Aqabah, then left, and some of them said: He did not stop. Ibn Musahir added: He threw seven pebbles at her, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble. (Abu Dawud 1961, Ibn Majah 3028)"
"13579","(13579) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Day of Departure shall not be held at The stones"
"13580","(13580) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: He will stand there lightly."
"13581","(13581) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I saw Al-Qasim standing at the pebbles on the day of the battle, and praying. It is made lighter, and before that it was made longer."
"13582","(13582) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, who said: It was said: To Abdullah: Some people were throwing pebbles at the top of it, so he went into the valley and then said: Who is here? By Him there is no god but Him. He threw away the stone upon which Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed. (Bukhari 1747, Muslim 307)"
"13583","(13583) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, who said: I performed Hajj with Omar for two years. One of them is in the year in which he was injured. All of that is performed until he stones Jamarat al-Aqaba from the depths of the valley."
"13584","(13584) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubair, on the authority of Jabir, who said: If you stone the Jamarat So he advanced to the bottom of the stream."
"13585","(13585) Azhar Al-Samman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Awn, who said: I saw Al-Qasim exploring the valley."
"13586","(13586) Abdul-A’la told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ata’, who said: It was more beloved to them that he stone it from the stomach. The valley"
"13587","(13587) Ibn Mushir and Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr bin Al-Ahwas. On the authority of his mother, she said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, throwing pebbles at Jamarat al-Aqaba from the depths of the valley."
"13588","(13588) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Bura, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab throwing stones at him. Jamarat al-Aqaba from above."
"13589","(13589) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: How do I stone the two long Jamarat? He said: The highest of them, then you branch out."
"13590","(13590) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar, a sheikh from the people of Basra, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to throw stones at the Jamarat from above."
"13591","(13591) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Rawasi told us, on the authority of Zuhayr, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah’s companions; They used to stone the first two Jamarat from above, throwing at the highest part of them."
"13592","(13592) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, who said: Throw them from where facilitated"
"13593","(13593) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Al-Qasim, Saleem, and Beneficiary throwing from the tree. Al-Qasim used to stand between it and Mecca, making Mecca behind his back his destination. As for Salim and Nafi’ They were two people who were lower in status than him."
"13594","(13594) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Bara’ bin Sulaym, who said: I asked the arbitrator, “Where should I throw at the Jamarat?” He said: Its origin."
"13595","(13595) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I saw Al-Qasim facing her and throwing her legs."
"13596","(13596) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; He used to start by stoning the first Jamarat, and he would stone the middle Jamarat, and he would stone the first Jamarat, and he would stone the subsequent Jamarat wherever it was. He came closer to him"
"13597","(13597) Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Al-Aswad said: When he crosses the tree, he throws the burning coal from under one of its branches."
"13598","(13598) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He used to say about a woman: If she menstruates after circumambulating the Kaaba several times: She should stay until she is pure and comes Tawaf"
"13599","(13599) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a woman performs three circumambulations and then onwards, then she menstruates, It suffices."
"13600","(13600) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: A woman should circumambulate three times and then menstruate. He said: She should observe it."
"13601","(13601) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Iyas, who said: I asked Ibrahim about a man who circumambulated At home, so there was some remaining time for her circumambulation, and she broke the fast, or a woman circumambulated and then menstruated, and there was some remaining time for her circumambulation, Where do you receive from? He said: From where she had her period."
"13602","(13602) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Performing the tawaaf is dearest to me, and if you do that, there is no problem with it."
"13603","(13603) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He used to pluck hair from his eyes while he was in ihram."
"13604","(13604) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said regarding Muharram: If he plucks his armpits, or trims his nails, then he must pay a ransom."
"13605","(13605) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who narrated it, saying: Whose family is inferior to The miqat is celebrated from wherever it is established, until that comes to the people of Mecca."
"13606","(13606) Muhammad bin Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, Ata’, and Mujahid, who said: If his family is among The time and between Mecca, a family from its people."
"13607","(13607) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he saw no harm if his family was inferior to him. The meeqat is to enter ihram from one’s family."
"13608","(13608) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If its family is below the miqaat, then it is Where He is created."
"13609","(13609) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man forgets to stone Jamrat al-Aqabah on the day of He slaughtered until the evening, he threw it away from the next day, and for that he shed blood."
"13610","(13610) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to say: If he leaves a hot coal He left the grave until nightfall intentionally, and there was blood on it, and he said: He should stone it the next day."
"13611","(13611) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I asked al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who forgot a pebble, or Two pebbles, or an ember, or two coals? They said: He will shed blood."
"13612","(13612) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who neglects to stone one Jamarat, he said: He feeds a poor person."
"13613","(13613) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he said: I don’t care. I threw Six or seven stones. Ibn Abbas said: In pre-Islamic times we stoned seven stones, and seven stones in Islam."
"13614","(13614) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; Regarding whoever throws a six, Tawus said: He gives something in charity."
"13615","(13615) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Saad, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: There is nothing wrong with him."
"13616","(13616) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa’id, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who threw five pebbles? He said: He should throw what remains, unless the days of Tashreeq have passed, and if the days of Tashreeq have passed, he will burn. That's why blood."
"13617","(13617) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who stones stones of stones with six stones, he said: He will resume."
"13618","(13618) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He hated to throw pebbles that had been thrown at him."
"13619","(13619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Shoot, if you wish, with what he once threw."
"13620","(13620) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, who said: He was forced to do so, or he was forced to do so. He throws pebbles at the pebbles that he stoned with."
"13621","(13621) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said: Did pebbles fall, or pebbles? He said: Take it from under your feet."
"13622","(13622) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amir Al-Aslami, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When We reached Wadi Muhassir. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Take the pebbles for the pebbles from Wadi Muhassir."
"13623","(13623) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: He used to carry pebbles from Muzdalifah to throw stones. The stones"
"13624","(13624) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abdul-Malik, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr said to us: Take the pebbles from the Wherever you want."
"13625","(13625) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: The one who throws stones takes pebbles from a group."
"13626","(13626) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Take it from Muzdalifah."
"13627","(13627) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr; He was carrying the pebbles of the Jamarat from Muzdalifah."
"13628","(13628) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Take it from wherever you wish."
"13629","(13629) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He used to take the pebbles for the pebbles from Muzdalifah."
"13630","(13630) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, who said: We used to collect pebbles for the lions. We are setting off for Arafat."
"13631","(13631) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, on the authority of his father, he said: I narrated with Abdullah, when we reached the Jamarat, he said: The Qat is for you, so I handed him seven pebbles."
"13632","(13632) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Take the pebbles of the Jamarat from wherever you wish."
"13633","(13633) Ismail Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Al-Husayn, he said: Abu Al-Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me the following morning: “Strike pebbles.” He said: So I struck him. Pebbles like gravel, and he said: Like these, throw them away. (Nasa’i 4065. Ahmad 1/347)"
"13634","(13634) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he will respond and say: At your command, O God, at your command, you have no partner. Indeed, praise is And the blessings and dominion are yours, you have no partner. (Bukhari 1549, Abu Dawud 1808)"
"13635","(13635) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, and Yahya bin Sa’id, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, likewise. (Muslim 842)"
"13636","(13636) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, claimed monotheism: At your service, O God, at your service, at your service, you have no partner. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours and the kingdom, you have no partner."
"13637","(13637) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Atiyya, on the authority of Aisha, She said: I learned from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as he used to recite: At your service, O God, at your command, at your service, no. Your partner is yours. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours. (Bukhari 1550, Ahmad 6/230)"
"13638","(13638) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning the Talbiyah like this, meaning like the saying of Jabir on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: Go to her, For it is the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"13639","(13639) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Taghlib, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yazid said: Abdullah used to say in his talbiyah: At your command, O God, at your command, there is no partner with you. Laklaka, indeed praise and blessings are yours and dominion, and he says, “This is how the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to respond to you.” And he greeted you.\n(Muslim 2700, Ahmad 1/410)"
"13640","(13640) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Salamah, who said: Saad bin Abi Waqqas heard a man He said: Labbayk, the Dhul-Maaraj. So Saad said: Labbaik, Dhaul-Maaraj. Indeed, he is the Dhul-Maaraj, and we did not say that about Ali. The era of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Ahmad 1/172, Abu Ali 720)"
"13641","(13641) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abi Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Fadl, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said regarding his talbiyah: He answered you, the truth has answered you. \n(Ahmad 2/776, Tayalisi 2377)"
"13642","(13642) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Yazeed, he said: Abdullah was This talbiyah teaches us: At your command, O God, at your command. Indeed, praise and blessings are Yes"
"13643","(13643) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Khaythamiya, he said: They used to say these three, he said: And it was the black He says it, and Yazid says: By the kingdom, you have no partner."
"13644","(13644) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Omar passed on the eve of the day of Arafah. On a red camel, and the head of its mount was shortened to the point that it almost hit the captains of the travellers. He said: And he recites the Talbiyah with three times; At your service, O God, at your service, at your service, there is no partner at your service. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours, and it was as easy as the neck. And when he passed one of the ropes, he raised his hand and said “Allahu Akbar.”"
"13645","(13645) Abdou and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar bin Makhramah, he said: Omar’s prayer was: Here you are, O God, here you are, here you are, there is no partner with you. Indeed, praise and blessings are yours. By the kingdom, I have no partner with you. You are hereby, desired and feared. You are hereby, possessor of blessings and good bounty.\n Abdou said: Hisham said: He will begin that and repeat it.\n Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar added: He said: My father - meaning Hisham on the authority of his father - used to recite the Talbiyah in the same way, except that Abu Khaled did not say: He begins that and repeats it."
"13646","(13646) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, who said: Ibn Umar used to visit Zayd from him: At Your command, my desires and deeds are at Your command."
"13647","(13647) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yahya, and Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I caught them from... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: At your command, O God, at your command. You have no partner. Indeed, praise is And the blessings are yours and the kingdom, you have no partner. He said: Ibn Umar Yazid said: And the desires are yours and the deeds are with you. I am happy with you"
"13648","(13648) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It is as if I am looking at And the scent of perfume came from the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Muharram. (Bukhari 271. Muslim 847)"
"13649","(13649) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It is as if I am looking And the scent of perfume was in the joints of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he was making his welcome. (Muslim 848)"
"13650","(13650) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to apply perfume before entering ihram, and the effects of the perfume would be seen in his parts after That is for three. (Nasa’i 3683. Ibn Majah 2928)"
"13651","(13651) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha; When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to enter ihram, he would apply the best oil he could find, until he saw And his hair is in his beard and his head. (Nasa’i 3680)"
"13652","(13652) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Aisha: About something? Did you please the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: With the best perfume, and she said: When it is permissible before it enters into ihram.\n(Bukhari 5930, Muslim 37)"
"13653","(13653) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: I saw A ray of goodness in the departures of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, after three days, while he was in Muharram. (Nasa’i 3682)"
"13654","(13654) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; She spread out her hands and said: I applied perfume to him with the hands of these two forbidden things when he entered ihram, and with his place before he circumambulated the Kaaba. (Bukhari 1539. Tirmidhi 917)"
"13655","(13655) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Muslim Al-Bateen; When Al-Hussein bin Ali entered ihram, he would anoint himself with oil, and he would anoint his companions with perfume or apply perfume."
"13656","(13656) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hashim bin Hashim, on the authority of Aisha bin Saad, who said: Saad used to perfume himself with Entering ihram with offspring."
"13657","(13657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays, on the authority of al-Shu`bi, who said: Abdullah ibn Ja`far used to use musk, then He puts it on his mouth before entering ihram."
"13658","(13658) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Kathir bin Sam, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafiyyah; He used to wrap his head with a new blanket if he wanted to enter ihram."
"13659","(13659) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Asama, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his mother, who said: I saw Aisha making fun of At its exits, perfume before it enters ihram, then it enters ihram."
"13660","(13660) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Muslim bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, that He used to anoint himself with salkha when entering ihram."
"13661","(13661) Hammad bin Masadi narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Hafs, on the authority of Uthman bin Urwah, who said: Urwah used to burn coals. He would wear his clothes for dinner, and he would not stop there until he went to the mosque and entered ihram there. He said: And he would see lava dripping from the water. Most importantly, we are in ihram, so this is not objectionable to us."
"13662","(13662) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: I saw Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr with his head And his beard is made of perfume, and he is in ihram. If it had belonged to a man, he would have taken capital from it."
"13663","(13663) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah; Ibn al-Zubayr used to wear a new garment when entering ihram."
"13664","(13664) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: My father used to perfume himself with offspring when entering ihram. And milk."
"13665","(13665) Abdah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders; Ibn Abbas did not see anything wrong with using perfume during his ihram, and on the Day of Sacrifice before he visited you."
"13666","(13666) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I will listen to him. In my head before I enter into ihram, and I like it to remain. Ibn al-Zubayr said: I do not see any harm in it, and Ibn Umar said: I do not order it, nor do I He forbade it."
"13667","(13667) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A man applies everything to himself when entering ihram. Except for the feminine, the feminine feminine: “al-sāriyya” and “al-malaab.”"
"13668","(13668) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It is as if I am looking And the scent of perfume was in the mouths of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was reciting the Talbiyah. (Muslim 41. Ahmad 207)"
"13669","(13669) Waki’ told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwah told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I used to perfume The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he entered ihram, as best as I can. (Ahmad 6/207 Ibn Hibban 3772)"
"13670","(13670) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Amr narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Aisha, she said: I congratulated the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his ihram when he entered ihram, and for his ihram when he entered ihram, before he circumambulated the Kaaba."
"13671","(13671) Abu Usama and Waki` told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubair; He used to perfume himself with new perfume when he entered ihram."
"13672","(13672) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Alqamiya and Al-Aswad were pilgrims with Abdullah bin Al-Harith, brother of Al-Ashtar, was sufficient for their expenses."
"13673","(13673) Al-Bakrawi narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Muhammad narrated to us, he said: They were the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Some of them perform Hajj with others, and that is sufficient for them."
"13674","(13674) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Aslam, the client of Omar; Omar smelled a sweet scent while he was in Dhul-Halif, so he said: Who is this from? Muawiyah said: From me, and he said: Is your security for my life? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, do not be hasty with me, for the mother of my beloved has given me kindness and swore by me. He said: And I swear to you. You will return to her, and she will wash it for yourself just as she cleansed you. He said: So he returned to her until he joined them some way."
"13675","(13675) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Omar called for a garment, and he was brought a garment containing a pleasant fragrance, and he returned it."
"13676","(13676) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Sa`d bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father; That Abraham saw a man who had applied perfume when entering ihram, so he ordered him to wash his head with clay."
"13677","(13677) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Uyaynah ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, who said: I performed Hajj once, and I agreed with Abd al-Rahman. Ibn Amr Ibn Al-Aas, when it was at Ihram, we poured some perfume, and Abdul Rahman said to me: I wish you had not done that. I once performed Hajj with Uthman bin Abi Al-Aas, and he entered ihram from Al-Manjashaniyah, and he was near Al-Basra, and he said to us: On you. With this white clay, wash your heads with it when entering ihram."
"13678","(13678) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated for a man to use perfume when he was in ihram."
"13679","(13679) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like that, he likes to come disheveled and dusty."
"13680","(13680) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He disliked perfume when in ihram, and said: If there is any of it in it, let him wash it and clean it."
"13681","(13681) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; If he wanted to enter ihram, he would leave his clothes uncovered fifteen days before that."
"13682","(13682) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; It was disliked for the ihram, when he was in ihram, to apply oil that contained musk, or mouths, or perfume."
"13683","(13683) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, that Sa’id ibn Jubair used to avoid perfume when he wanted to. To be forbidden."
"13684","(13684) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Wabara, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab found a smell at Ihram, so her companion made a threat, so Muawiyah returned and threw away the blanket she was wearing, meaning his perfume."
"13685","(13685) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar and Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, He said: I heard Ibn Umar say: To be daubed with tar is more beloved to me than to be daubed in ihram. I apply perfume."
"13686","(13686) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar al-Ansari, he said: When they entered ihram, he found Omar smelled a good smell, so he said: Who is this smell from? Al-Bara’ bin Azib said: From me, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: We know that your wife is a perfumer, or a perfumer, but the pilgrim The dustiest excrement."
"13687","(13687) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who gets some of the perfume from the Kaaba as his share? He said: It will not harm him."
"13688","(13688) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salih bin Hayyan, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik whose garment was stained with something. The Kaaba was in ihram, but he did not wash it."
"13689","(13689) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Jafar, who said: I saw Ibn Umar leaving the Kaaba, and his chest was stained. Of her goodness."
"13690","(13690) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I saw in the dress of Amr bin Shuaib a deterrent from the appearance of the Kaaba. So I said to him: What is this in your dress while you are in ihram? He said: This is not disliked here. It was called Bakka because people cry over it."
"13691","(13691) Ali bin Hashim and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He does not enter Mecca. No one without Ihram, except for lumberjacks, workers, and utility owners."
"13692","(13692) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Ali, who said: Do not enter it except in a state of ihram. It means Mecca."
"13693","(13693) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to enter Mecca without being in Ihram."
"13694","(13694) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They liked not to enter Mecca. Except for those in ihram."
"13695","(13695) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: No one is permitted to enter Mecca except in a state of ihram, and it was Abd al-Malik gives licenses to woodcutters there."
"13696","(13696) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man entering Mecca without being in Ihram. ? The arbitrator hated him, but Hammad saw no harm in him."
"13697","(13697) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujair, on the authority of Tawus; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, never entered Mecca except in a state of ihram, except on the day of the conquest of Mecca."
"13698","(13698) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Do not enter Mecca except in a state of ihram."
"13699","(13699) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: Do not enter Mecca except in a state of ihram."
"13700","(13700) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He stayed in Mecca, then went out to go to Medina, until, just as he was still there, he heard that there was an army from the armies of temptation. They entered Medina, but he did not want to enter upon them, so he returned to Mecca and entered it without ihram."
"13701","(13701) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Jafar, who said: My father and Amr bin Dinar went out to their land, leaving the Sacred Mosque. Then they entered Mecca without ihram."
"13702","(13702) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Malik Ibn Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no harm in him."
"13703","(13703) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, circumambulated in He performed Hajj for a week and prayed two rak'ahs, and this is what he did during his lifetime. He said: If a man performs Tawaf, I would not like him to do more than that. Two rak'ahs, and if he adds more, there is no problem with him, but if he finds the Ka'bah open, then he should not enter it until he has circumambulated between the two rows. And the marwa."
"13704","(13704) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Salim bin Hayyan narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Qatn narrated to us, on the authority of Maya Bint. Mahrez, she said: I heard Omar bin Al-Khattab saying: Perform the Hajj on this offspring, and do not eat its provisions, and leave behind its slaves. In her necks."
"13705","(13705) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man does not have to perform Hajj with his wife unless If He wills. Al-Awza’i said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir said: It is upon her if she has not performed Hajj. Makhoul said: You must perform Hajj. Your women"
"13706","(13706) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was It is chained in Al-Safa and Al-Marwah, and it stops at Al-Marwah Al-Bayda."
"13707","(13707) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, he said: Tell me who saw Uthman. Ibn Affan standing at the lower basin of Safa."
"13708","(13708) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Sabit; Omar used to place what looked like a camel’s clod on his right thigh, meaning in the marwa."
"13709","(13709) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; That his father used to stand at the marrow, next to what looked like a camel’s trough, and in Safa in the dug-out place."
"13710","(13710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ikrimah; He used to stand below the one as if it were a camel's paw, and he would stand from Al-Safa, lower than the pitted place."
"13711","(13711) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: He ascends Safa until He looks at the house."
"13712","(13712) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Rabah bin Abi Marouf, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He disliked a man standing at the door of the mosque if he wanted to go to his family, leaning towards the Kaaba. to it and supplicate, and said: The Jews do that."
"13713","(13713) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I heard him and he saw a man turning to him. The Kaaba was at the door of the mosque, so he forbade it and said: The Jews are doing this."
"13714","(13714) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Umari, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was imitating and feeling like the ally."
"13715","(13715) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, who said: My father used to say: If a man gives a gift, he will feel it. Where it is forbidden."
"13716","(13716) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to feel the Day of Tarwiyah. And before that"
"13717","(13717) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He could feel his body with his knowledge."
"13718","(13718) Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, he said: I love to feel At Arafat."
"13719","(13719) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, and Ibn Al-Aswad; They both said: He is made to wear his hair, then he enters ihram."
"13720","(13720) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The body does not even feel He is forbidden."
"13721","(13721) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Fudayl, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If he says: On the day he will do such-and-such He is in ihram for Hajj. He said: If he breaks his oath, then he is in ihram. And if he says: If I do such-and-such, then I am in ihram for Hajj. Then he entered Shawwal. It is forbidden."
"13722","(13722) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: If he says: If I do such-and-such, then I am in ihram for Hajj, he said: He performs Hajj with the people."
"13723","(13723) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Similar to the hadith of Mujalid."
"13724","(13724) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a man who says: On the day he does such-and-such, he will be in ihram for Hajj on that day. If he breaks his oath, then he will be in ihram on that day. For Hajj, and if he says: If I do not do such-and-such, then I am in ihram for Hajj. He says: If he performs Hajj with the people, that is sufficient for him."
"13725","(13725) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: One time is sufficient. He says: I tell you on the authority of so-and-so."
"13726","(13726) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’; Like that"
"13727","(13727) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Layth, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They believed that forgiveness descends upon repulsion from He knew"
"13728","(13728) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They both said: If a man performs Hajj on behalf of another man and forgets to name him, then Hajj on his behalf is sufficient, for God Almighty knows from whom Hajj"
"13729","(13729) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, praised Umar, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, and the caliphs as well, and Ata’ said:"
"13730","(13730) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: I was informed on the authority of Al-Qasim and Salem that they were They say: When the people of Mecca go out to Mina, they stop. He said: And he was Ata, and Al-Zuhri say: They complete."
"13731","(13731) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He was staying in Mecca, so when he left for Mina, he shortened it."
"13732","(13732) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Hanzala, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about praying with the imam according to your knowledge? He said: Pray as he prayed, and I said: I am a Meccan. He said: I knew. He said: I asked Salim and Tawoos, and they said the same thing."
"13733","(13733) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata’; They said: The people of Mecca are not required to shorten prayers during Hajj."
"13734","(13734) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: No. Besiegement, except for one who has been imprisoned by an enemy. He said: And my father said: Today is not besiegement."
"13735","(13735) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no confinement except due to illness, or an enemy, or a matter. locked up"
"13736","(13736) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Musa bin Uqba, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: There is no siege except from Enemy"
"13737","(13737) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, who said: Everything in which a muhrim is detained is Blockade"
"13738","(13738) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no siege except as a result of war."
"13739","(13739) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Suwayd, who said: I heard Ibn Al-Zubair, he said: The enjoyment of life is only To Hajj, when a man performs the Hajj and is confined to it, either by illness, or an enemy, or something that detains him."
"13740","(13740) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Sabit; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions used to cut the left hand of the animal and slaughter it standing on it. What remains of its lists? (Abu Dawud 1764)"
"13741","(13741) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to slaughter her while she was being slaughtered on her right hand."
"13742","(13742) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Use whichever hand you wish."
"13743","(13743) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to use the left-handed mind."
"13744","(13744) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In terms of the body, how do you slaughter? He said: You should cut her left hand and slaughter her with her right hand."
"13745","(13745) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to hold her left hand when he wanted to slaughter her."
"13746","(13746) Abdullah bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He did not leave the mosque until he had said the greeting, whether he was performing tawaaf or not tawaaf."
"13747","(13747) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whenever you enter the Sacred Mosque, you circumambulate At home, or if you do not circumambulate, then face the stone when you want to leave the mosque, or face it, then say “Allahu Akbar” and pray to God."
"13748","(13748) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Hafsiya, who said: I went around with Sa`id ibn Jubayr, and when he passed by He turned to him with a stone but did not greet him."
"13749","(13749) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, who said: I circumambulated with a peacock, and perhaps he did not receive any of the pillars. Until he leaves."
"13750","(13750) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of his father; He used to circumambulate the Kaaba, but not face-to-face."
"13751","(13751) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, and more, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw And he greeted a man who was leading between two men - and Yazid said: between his two sons - and he said: What is this? They said: He vowed to walk, and he said: God Almighty is not sufficient to torment this man, so let him ride. Except that Yazid said: On the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas.\n(Tirmidhi 1537)"
"13752","(13752) Abu Khalid and Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Zuhar, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Ra’aniyi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Malik, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amir Al-Jihani, who said: My sister vowed to walk to... Is the House of God barefoot and not covered with veils? So I asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Order your sister to cover herself and ride, and to fast for three days.\n(Tirmidhi 1544, Abu Dawud 3286)"
"13753","(13753) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ali, He said: If walking is made upon him and he is not able, then let him lean his body and ride."
"13754","(13754) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Concerning a man who walked half the way in a vow, then rode. He said: He comes from Qabil and rides as long as he walks, and walks as long as he rides. And he slaughters a body."
"13755","(13755) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who vowed to perform Hajj walking, he said: He walks until when he becomes tired, he rides and leads."
"13756","(13756) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He walks, and if his knee is broken, he will support his body."
"13757","(13757) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Amr bin Saeed Al-Bajli, who said: I was under the pulpit of Ibn Al-Zubayr was on his way, then a man came and said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have vowed to perform Hajj on foot, even when Such and such. I was afraid that I would miss Hajj, so I rode. He said: There is no sin on you. Come back a year ago and walk as long as you rode. And ride as long as you walk."
"13758","(13758) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who was assigned to walk, and he walked part of the way, and rode part, and said: He should look at what he rode, then assess his recompense. He bought it and gave it as a gift. He said: If he does not reach the age, give it in charity to the poor."
"13759","(13759) Zayd bin Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I heard Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt saying: He rides and guides his body, and Al-Qasim said: If he is facing, then let him walk as long as he rides."
"13760","(13760) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, and Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Urwah ibn Udhaynah, Malik said: I found him, and Ubayd Allah said: His mother was made to walk, so she walked until when she reached the watering can, she was unable. So Ibn Umar was asked? He said: She was told to return next year and walk from where she was unable."
"13761","(13761) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Habib ibn Abi Marzuq, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If any woman is made obligated to walk home and is not able, let her ride and let her body grow."
"13762","(13762) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; He did not see any problem when he came from Arafat, taking another route to the left and to the right."
"13763","(13763) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, or Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in taking another route from Mina, when he left Arafat, the Dhabi route."
"13764","(13764) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They both said: There is blood in three hairs, both the forgetful and the intentional."
"13765","(13765) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Its majesty will be removed, do not wallow in it, meaning The body"
"13766","(13766) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Indeed, he would not slaughter her while her majesty was upon her."
"13767","(13767) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Layla. On the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to take care of his body, and he commanded me not to give it to the butcher. He took something from it and said: We will give it to you from Ourselves. (Bukhari 1716, Muslim 954)"
"13768","(13768) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, who said: Do not give the butcher’s musk to the slaughterer. And if you find a sheep, buy a sheep with it, and slaughter it."
"13769","(13769) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in giving the butcher’s musk to him."
"13770","(13770) Zaid bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Hamid Al-Tawil, on the authority of Abdullah bin Ubaid bin Umair. He said: There is no harm in giving the butcher her skin."
"13771","(13771) Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Saif, he said: I was informed on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The butcher is not given any of it. Something"
"13772","(13772) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Abi Muslim, on the authority of Tawoos. Some of our companions said: It is on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The people were leaving in every direction, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one should leave until... It will be his last covenant with the House. (Muslim 963. Abu Dawud 1995)"
"13773","(13773) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, and Ata’; Omar used to return those who left, but it was not the last time he stayed at the House."
"13774","(13774) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: No one should be alienated. Until he circumambulates the Kaaba, for the last ritual ritual is circumambulation of the Kaaba."
"13775","(13775) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The people were commanded to be End their vow of the House, and ease the burden of menstruation. (Muslim 380)"
"13776","(13776) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawus, who said: They used to flee from me. Then it was said to them: This will be the last of your covenant with the House, and menstruation was granted."
"13777","(13777) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Kilab ibn Ali, on the authority of Mansour ibn Abi Sulaiman, on the authority of my nephew Jubayr bin Mutim, on the authority of Jubayr bin Mutim, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood on the Marwa with a ripper in his hand. He shortens some of his hair and says: She entered her life in Hajj until the Day of Resurrection, and there is no conversion to Islam. The camels will cry loudly, and they will shout “Allahu Akbar” loudly."
"13778","(13778) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The companions of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, made it lawful. He said hello and they cut their hair short, but did not shave."
"13779","(13779) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I used to perform Hajj with my father and perform Umrah, and a group of people went to My shoulder, and he never ordered me to shave it when I was shortening it."
"13780","(13780) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man performs Hajj the first time, he shave, and if he performs Hajj another time, If he wishes, he may shave, and if he wishes, he may shorten his hair, and shaving is better. If a man performs Umrah and has never performed Hajj, then if he wishes, he may shave, and if he wishes, he may shorten his hair. He was enjoying his hair. He shortened his hair and then shaved his hair."
"13781","(13781) Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Habib the teacher, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about his hair: should he be shaved, or should he be cut short? He said: Yes, that is what he wants. If he wants, he should shave his head, and if he wants, he should cut his hair short."
"13782","(13782) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning one who has never performed Hajj: If he wishes, he may shave the shave, and if he wishes, he may shorten his hair."
"13783","(13783) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad; Alqamah and Al-Aswad performed Hajj, or one of them performed Hajj, or the other performed Umrah, so one of them shaved his hair and the other cut his hair."
"13784","(13784) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to love to shave at the beginning of Hajj, and the beginning of life."
"13785","(13785) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Ja’far; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, shaved his head during his lifetime."
"13786","(13786) Bishr bin Al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Amr bin Sahl, he said: I saw Othman approaching Mecca and we were with him, but he will not untie her until he leaves, or more. He must circumambulate the House, perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwa, and shave his head."
"13787","(13787) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He shaved his life."
"13788","(13788) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he performs Umrah and has never performed Hajj, then if he wishes, he may shorten his hair, and if he wishes, he may shave the shave."
"13789","(13789) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They used to prefer for a man the first He is required to shave for Hajj, and the first thing he performs Umrah is to shave."
"13790","(13790) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Amara bin Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O God, forgive those who cut their hair, they said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said: Oh God, forgive those who cut their hair three times. They said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said: And for those who fall short. (Bukhari 1728, Muslim 320)"
"13791","(13791) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Wahb bin Abdullah, he saw it on the authority of His father, he said: I was with my father and I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying with his hand: May God have mercy on those who shave, so he said Man: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said in the third: And those who fall short. (Ahmad 6/393, Hamidi 931)"
"13792","(13792) Yazid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Hisham Al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like it (Ahmad 3/20. Tayalisi 2224)"
"13793","(13793) Yazeed told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ishaq told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, forgive those who shave. He said it three times. He said: So they said: O Messenger of God, What is the matter with those who shave their heads when they show compassion? He said: They did not complain. (Ibn Majah 3045. Ahmad 1/353)"
"13794","(13794) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: And peace be upon him: May God have mercy on those who cut their hair, they said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said in the third: And those who fall short.\n(Bukhari 1727, Muslim 316)"
"13795","(13795) Waki` and Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Yahya bin al-Husayn, on the authority of his grandmother; She heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, supplicate three times for those who shave their hair, and once for those who cut their hair once. Waki` did not say: regarding the Farewell Pilgrimage.\n(Muslim 946. Ahmad 4/70)"
"13796","(13796) Ubayd Allah told us, he said: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Habashi ibn Junadahi, he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: O God, forgive those who cut their hair, they said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said: Oh God, forgive those who cut their hair. They said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said: Forgive those who are negligent. (Ahmad 4/1451 Tabarani 3510)"
"13797","(13797) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Aws bin Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Burayd bin Abi Maryam, on the authority of Malik bin Spring The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O God, forgive those who cut their hair three times, they said: O Messenger of God, and those who are negligent? He said: And those who fall short. At that time I had a shaved head, but I was not pleased with shaving my head with red camels, or he said: a great danger. Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Yunus told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Baqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abd told us Allah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah Al-Absi, said: (Ahmad 4/177 at-Tabarani 604)"
"13798","(13798) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever performs Umrah after Hajj will receive reward on his head. The Moses"
"13799","(13799) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq; He was asked about a man who performed Umrah and shaved, then performed Hajj? He said: He passes a razor over his head."
"13800","(13800) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyash, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A razor passes over his head."
"13801","(13801) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I heard him asked about the one who will perform Umrah after Hajj? He said: He passes a razor over his head."
"13802","(13802) Hafs told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Ata’; What about the old sheikh performing Hajj while he is bald? He said: Pass the razor over his head."
"13803","(13803) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Nafi’, on the authority of his father, who said: Ibn Umar was a bald man, so whenever he performed Hajj, he would He made the Umrah with a razor on his head."
"13804","(13804) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Umar; {"
"13805","(13805) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Shawwal and Dhul-Qa’di. And Dhul-Hijjah"
"13806","(13806) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Shawwal and Dhul-Qa’dah. And Dhul-Hijjah"
"13807","(13807) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; Like him"
"13808","(13808) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Shawwal, Dhul-Qa’dah, and the beginning of Dhul-Hijjah."
"13809","(13809) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad; Like him"
"13810","(13810) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: Abdullah said: {Hajj is in known months} He said: Shawwal Dhul-Qa'dah, and the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah."
"13811","(13811) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; In the Almighty’s saying: {Hajj is a known month} He said: Shawwal, Dhul-Qa’dah, and Dhul-Hijjah."
"13812","(13812) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; (Hajj is a known month) He said: Shawwal, Dhul-Qa’dah, and Dhul-Hijjah."
"13813","(13813) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa`dah, and the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah. Hajj"
"13814","(13814) Waki’ told us, and Yahya bin Adam, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {The Hajj is known months} He said: Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa`dah, and the ten days of Dhul-Hijjah."
"13815","(13815) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Bais bin Fadan, on the authority of Abu Shaykh al-Hana’i, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about God Almighty says: {Hajj is a well-known month}? He said: Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'dah, and Dhul-Hijjah."
"13816","(13816) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Ibn Abbas: (So whoever made Hajj obligatory in it) said: Talbiyah."
"13817","(13817) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hussein bin Aqeel, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He said: Ihram."
"13818","(13818) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; {So whoever makes the Hajj obligatory therein} He said: Whoever makes the Hajj obligatory therein."
"13819","(13819) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The obligatory prayer is the Talbiyah."
"13820","(13820) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Ilal is obligatory for Hajj."
"13821","(13821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; {So whoever makes Hajj obligatory therein} He said: Talbiyah."
"13822","(13822) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; {So whoever makes Hajj obligatory therein} He said: Talbiyah."
"13823","(13823) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah; (So whoever makes Hajj obligatory therein) he said: Talbiyah."
"13824","(13824) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; {So whoever makes the Hajj obligatory therein} He said: Al-Hilal."
"13825","(13825) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Marzban, on the authority of Abu Aoun, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr; (So whoever makes Hajj obligatory therein) he said: Al-Hilal."
"13826","(13826) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Jabir ibn Abdullah, who said: He came to the Prophet A man, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: O Messenger of God, tell me about the Umrah, is it obligatory? He said: No, but it is better for you to perform Umrah. (Tirmidhi 931, Ahmad 3/316)"
"13827","(13827) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salih Mahan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He said: Hajj is jihad, and Umrah is voluntary. (Tabarani 11)"
"13828","(13828) Ibn Idris and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Abdullah said: Hajj is obligatory, and Umrah is voluntary."
"13829","(13829) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: It is voluntary."
"13830","(13830) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about the Umrah, is it obligatory? He said: There has been disagreement about it."
"13831","(13831) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Umrah is a Sunnah, and it is not By obligation"
"13832","(13832) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He recited {And complete the Hajj}, then he stopped, then said: {And the life is for Allah}"
"13833","(13833) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, Tawoos, and Mujahid. They said: Hajj and Umrah are two obligatory duties."
"13834","(13834) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: It is obligatory."
"13835","(13835) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He is not of the creation of God Almighty. No one but Hajj and Umrah are obligatory upon him."
"13836","(13836) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr was asked about the Umrah, and is it obligatory? He said: Yes."
"13837","(13837) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Saeed bin Jubayr and Ali bin Hussein were asked about Al-Umri. Is it obligatory? So they recited these verses: {And complete the Hajj and the Umrah}"
"13838","(13838) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I asked Ata’, I said: Is the Umrah obligatory? He said: Yes."
"13839","(13839) Abdullah bin Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudail bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: Al-Umrah, the minor Hajj."
"13840","(13840) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; Concerning the one who performs Umrah before performing Hajj, he said: We pray for God’s sake, He will not harm you whichever way you begin."
"13841","(13841) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Masruq, who said: You were commanded to perform Hajj and Umrah."
"13842","(13842) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; They said: Hajj and Umrah are two obligatory duties."
"13843","(13843) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: The Umrah is obligatory."
"13844","(13844) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I asked Abdullah bin Shaddad about the greater Hajj? He said: The greater Hajj is on the Day of Sacrifice, and the lesser Hajj is the Umrah."
"13845","(13845) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: It was said: Al-Umrah. The Minor Hajj"
"13846","(13846) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Hayyan bin Umair, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We sacrifice ourselves for the sake of Allah. upon you, and it will not harm you whichever way you start."
"13847","(13847) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The Umrah is the lesser Hajj."
"13848","(13848) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan used to say: Mut’i’ is part of the Umrah."
"13849","(13849) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, he said: I said to Ata’: Will it be sufficient for us of what was imposed on us, meaning Umrah, enjoyment? He said: Yes."
"13850","(13850) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: Umrah is obligatory, and it is sufficient for enjoyment."
"13851","(13851) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, and Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever performs Hajj before dawn comes has performed Hajj, and whoever misses it Arafat missed Hajj."
"13852","(13852) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Like him (Daraqutni 21)"
"13853","(13853) Abu Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikki, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn al-Zubair. They said: Who He had intercourse with Arafah at night, thus completing the Hajj."
"13854","(13854) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hussein bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Who He stopped at Arafat at night, then he has performed Hajj, if he is pious and righteous."
"13855","(13855) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah bin Omar, He said: If a man stops at Arafat at night, his Hajj is complete, even if the people do not reach you in a crowd."
"13856","(13856) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, and Sulayman ibn Yasar, And Ata bin Abi Rabah, and Salem bin Abdullah; They said: If he stops at Arafat at night, he has performed Hajj, but if he does not, the people have gathered together."
"13857","(13857) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Salem, who said: Whoever stops at Arafat at night has completed Hajj. Even if the people do not catch up with you in droves."
"13858","(13858) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Whoever performs the waqf at Arafah at night before dawn comes. He has performed the Hajj, and whoever has not performed it, he should circumambulate the Kaaba and walk between Safa and Marwa, and shave his head. It is permissible, and he may perform Hajj the following year and make a sacrifice. If that is not possible, then he must fast for three days during the Hajj and seven days when he returns."
"13859","(13859) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They both said: If a man stands at Arafat before dawn on the night of Sacrifice, then he has performed Hajj, even if the people have not performed it. In plural"
"13860","(13860) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever misses it will be known to him, or a group of people will miss it. Hajj"
"13861","(13861) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Whoever realizes his knowledge before the sunrise Fajr, Hajj has begun."
"13862","(13862) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Urwah bin Mudarris Al-Tai; He performed Hajj during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people did not reach you except when they were in a crowd. He said: So I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, so I said: O Messenger of God, I have exhausted myself and finished my mount, and by God I have not left a single rope. The ropes were standing on them, so is there any Hajj for me? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever prayed this prayer with us, and had previously departed from Arafat at night, or During the day, he completed his fasting and completed his Hajj. (Tirmidhi 891, Abu Dawud 1945)"
"13863","(13863) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Bukair ibn Ata’, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Umar, he said: I heard him. He says: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was standing at Arafah, and some people from Mecca came to him and said: Messenger of God, how is Hajj? He said: Hajj is known, so whoever comes before dawn on the night of congregation, his Hajj has been completed, of three days, so whoever hastens it Two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays it, there is no sin on him. Then a man comes behind him and calls for them.\n(Tirmidhi 889, Abu Dawud 1944)"
"13864","(13864) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, and Zaid; They said: In the case of a man who misses the Hajj: it is permissible for him to perform the Hajj, and he must perform the Hajj from before."
"13865","(13865) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever does not catch you will have to offer a blood sacrifice, and make it an ‘umrah, and he will have to perform Hajj from He met"
"13866","(13866) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Like him"
"13867","(13867) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; In the case of one who misses Hajj, he said: His Hajj is repeated as a lifetime."
"13868","(13868) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim; As for the one who misses the Hajj, he said: Make it an age, and he must perform the Hajj from the following year and give him a gift. If he does not find it, he fasts. Three days during the Hajj, and seven days when he returns."
"13869","(13869) Narrated by Gandar, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Haytham, on the authority of Talhih, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: If he misses the Hajj, he will make it an ‘umrah, and upon him is a sacrifice that is dearer to me."
"13870","(13870) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: He will make it a Umrah, and upon him. The gift and Hajj from the beginning."
"13871","(13871) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, he said: It is permissible Umrah, and he must perform Hajj from before."
"13872","(13872) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan ibn Amr, on the authority of Mihran Abi Safwan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever among you wants to perform Hajj, let him hasten. (Abu Dawud 1729. Ahmad 1/225)"
"13873","(13873) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Habib and his companions used to stay behind until some of Dhul-Qa’dah entered. God willing, Abraham thought of it."
"13874","(13874) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, who said: A peacock was presented in He is the first of the people, and he departs at the last of the people."
"13875","(13875) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Muhammad did not see any harm in a man buying a camel in a hurry. Aliyah"
"13876","(13876) Abu Asamah told us, on the authority of Buraid bin Abdullah, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Burda, who said: I swear to God that Hajj in Kufa, then I told the people about the situation on the eve of Arafat, but Abu Musa did not mind that."
"13877","(13877) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Burjan, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid; That he traveled from Basra to Mecca on the twelve or thirteen days. Doubt about me"
"13878","(13878) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, who said: Abdullah walked to us from Medina when he was killed. Omar in seven."
"13879","(13879) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He traveled from Mecca to Medina in three days, when the cry was called for Safiyyah."
"13880","(13880) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enjoyed it. Peace be upon him, Abu Bakr, Omar, Othman, and the first to prohibit it was Muawiyah. (Tirmidhi 822. Ahmad 1/292)"
"13881","(13881) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : I heard Omar saying: If I had performed Umrah, then performed Umrah, then performed Hajj, I would have enjoyed it."
"13882","(13882) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Omar bin Dhar, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Ibn Omar and Ibn Abbas were the first Enjoy."
"13883","(13883) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Ghunaim bin Qays, who said: I asked Sa’d about Mut’i, or About combining them? He said: We did this, and this is a disbeliever in the Lord of the Kaaba, or in the Lord of the Throne. That means Mu'awiyah. (Muslim 898)"
"13884","(13884) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Ma’n, who said: I heard Ibn Umar, Ibn al-Zubayr, Jabir bin Zayd, and Aba The lofty and the beautiful are commanded to enjoy the Hajj."
"13885","(13885) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The completion of Hajj is completed by the Umrah before it."
"13886","(13886) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Shu’ayb ibn al-Habhab, who said: Abu al-Aaliya commanded me to enjoy Hajj."
"13887","(13887) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Dinar, who said: I heard Ata’ ordering the enjoyment of Hajj."
"13888","(13888) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Abi al-Hakam, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: Where are you from Mut’i? You put two stitches in one stitch."
"13889","(13889) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Mujahid said: If I had performed Hajj from this land of yours, meaning Al-Kufa, seventy Hajjs, I would have added an Umrah for each Hajj. He said: So I said: Qiran? He said: No, he said: Make it a wet life."
"13890","(13890) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw it before he performed Hajj, even if a man had performed Hajj Twenty times"
"13891","(13891) Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bastam, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: If I had performed eighty Hajjs, I would have performed each Hajj. Enjoyable"
"13892","(13892) Mu’tamir ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: I performed forty Hajjs, and I did not leave except to perform Hajj."
"13893","(13893) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of Malik Ibn Dinar, who said: I asked eight people about Pleasure? All of them commanded me to do so: Al-Hasan, Ata’, Tawus, Jabir bin Zayd, Salim bin Abdullah, and Ikrimah. Mujahid and Al-Qasim."
"13894","(13894) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Dharr, he said: It was Enjoyment for the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, in particular. (Muslim 1600, Ibn Majah 2985)"
"13895","(13895) Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyash al-Amiri, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymimi, on the authority of Abiyya, on the authority of Abi Dharr, he said: We had a concession, meaning enjoyment in Hajj."
"13896","(13896) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, who said: I asked Alqamiya about the Mut’i during Hajj? He said: I did not feel that anyone would do it."
"13897","(13897) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He did not see the Mut’a before Hajj, and he would say: Start with Hajj and perform Umrah."
"13898","(13898) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: For the one being confined, and he recited these verses: {Then when you believe, then whoever enjoys the Umrah until the Hajj, then whatever is sufficient of the sacrifice}"
"13899","(13899) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdul Allah bin Khalid bin Asid, on the authority of Muharish Al-Kaabi; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Umrah from the scarab, and then he became a kaabait with the scarab. (Tirmidhi 935. An-Nasa’i 3846)"
"13900","(13900) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stayed for three days during his Umrah."
"13901","(13901) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of a sheikh from Banu Ghaffar from the people of Mecca, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi He said: When Abu Dharr entered Mecca, he would not stay there except for three days until he left, meaning for Hajj, or for Hajj. With your life"
"13902","(13902) Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Sahil, he said: I saw Othman approaching Mecca and we were with him, so what is the matter with her until he leaves? Nothing more. He must circumambulate the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwa."
"13903","(13903) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; It was desirable for the Muhrim to perform the prayer for three days."
"13904","(13904) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Like him"
"13905","(13905) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Ya’la bin Hakim; Omar bin Abdul Aziz came at night while he was performing Umrah, and he completed his Umrah during the night, then he left before the morning."
"13906","(13906) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They used to like to stay in Umrah is three."
"13907","(13907) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: The companions of Abdullah They stay for Umrah, complete the Tawaf, then leave for the night."
"13908","(13908) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik, who said: I saw Omar ibn Abd al-Aziz performing Hajj. Or he performs Umrah and only stays for three days until he leaves."
"13909","(13909) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, who said: I stayed with Al-Qasim bin Muhammad during Al-Umrah for three years."
"13910","(13910) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of his father; Omar stayed in Umrah for three nights."
"13911","(13911) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, who said: I heard our sheikhs mention that Asim bin Omar Ibn Al-Khattab used to come to Mecca for Umrah, but he would not leave his journey until he returned."
"13912","(13912) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Khaled bin Asid, on the authority of Muharish; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, performed the Umrah from the scarab, and then spent the morning with it as a turban. He said: And I saw its appearance as if it were a silver alloy."
"13913","(13913) Hafs ibn Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: The body should not be ridden unless it is tied or with a ring. Or scratched."
"13914","(13914) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is distilled and smeared if it is feared that it will destroy you."
"13915","(13915) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father; He used to snout his camel, and Ibn al-Zubayr used to do that."
"13916","(13916) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, who said: Strike the body and strike it."
"13917","(13917) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Thuwayr, on the authority of his father; Alqamah, Al-Aswad, and Amr bin Maymun did not accompany their camels."
"13918","(13918) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar used to walk to the Jamarat. He said: Ali bin Hussein was walking to it."
"13919","(13919) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He used to walk towards it, approaching and retreating."
"13920","(13920) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I noticed people walking and approaching. And we manage it."
"13921","(13921) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr throwing stones. Walking"
"13922","(13922) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ubaidah bin Nabil, who said: I saw Aisha bin Saad throwing stones. Livestock"
"13923","(13923) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He used to stone the Jamarat while walking, going and returning."
"13924","(13924) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was not necessary to walk to it. And he used to say: He did not ride while he was correct?!"
"13925","(13925) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir; He did not ride to the pebbles, except out of necessity."
"13926","(13926) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Muhammad bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of his father, who said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab He saw a man leading his wife onto a camel that was throwing stones at the Jamarat. He said: So he mounted the bike, denying that he was riding it."
"13927","(13927) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ayman bin Nabul, on the authority of Qadamah bin Abdullah, who said: I saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He stoned Jamrat al-Aqaba on the Day of Sacrifice on a she-camel of his companions. He was not beaten, nor was he expelled, nor is he to you.\n(Tirmidhi 903. Ahmad 3/412)"
"13928","(13928) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat on his camel. (Tirmidhi 899)"
"13929","(13929) Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, who said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyy throwing stones at The Jamarat is on Bardhun."
"13930","(13930) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Aaron bin Abi Ibrahim, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw Ibn Umar standing At the Jamarat on a donkey."
"13931","(13931) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Riding for two days. And he walked for two days."
"13932","(13932) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, who said: I saw Ata throwing stones at an animal, so I said to him? He said: I am an old man."
"13933","(13933) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He used to stone the Jamarat while he was riding."
"13934","(13934) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Abaya, he said: I saw Salim throwing the Jamarat while riding a donkey."
"13935","(13935) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Al-Qasim, who said: He used to come and stone the Jamarat on the day Al-Nahr, while he is riding."
"13936","(13936) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, he said: Amr told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I was among those who presented the Messenger of May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and his family’s weakness. (Muslim 303. Ibn Majah 3026)"
"13937","(13937) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Abi Yazeed told us; He heard Ibn Abbas say: I am among those who presented the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to his family in his double. (Bukhari 1478 and Abu Dawud 1934)"
"13938","(13938) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, and Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We presented the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to the slaves of Banu Abdul Muttalib over a group of reds, and he made He slaps our thighs and says: O my father, do not stone the Jamarat until the sun rises.\n Sufyan added: And I do not imagine anyone stoning it until the sun rises. (Abu Dawud 1935. Tahawi 217)"
"13939","(13939) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordered Umm Salama to perform the morning prayer in his prayers."
"13940","(13940) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Masoudi, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, presented twice as much to his family, and said: Do not stone the Jamarat until the sun rises. (Tirmidhi 893. Ahmad 1/344)"
"13941","(13941) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, saying: Amr bin Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of Salim bin Shawwal, on the authority of Umm Habiba, who said: We were We do it according to the covenant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Muslim 2991, Ahmad 426)"
"13942","(13942) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn al-Shawwal, he said: Abdullah bin Omar said; It is only the plural of a place from which you can depart whenever you wish."
"13943","(13943) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abdullah Mawla Asma’; She used to perform the Fajr prayer with maniyya."
"13944","(13944) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf; Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf used to hasten the women and children from the gathering at night."
"13945","(13945) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha; She used to offer her family’s double from the gathering at night. Ata’ said: And I will do it."
"13946","(13946) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to permit the old and the sick to break the fast from the congregation at night, but not to stone Jamarat al-Aqabah until The sun rises."
"13947","(13947) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A concession was granted to the sick person, the pregnant woman, and whoever had an illness. That they should disperse from the congregation at night, and not stone the Jamarat until the sun rises."
"13948","(13948) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah, he said: It was Ibn Umar. He will send his boys to the night of Muzdalifah, and they will perform the Fajr prayer at Mina, and stone the Jamarat before the people come."
"13949","(13949) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abul Zinad; Ibn Awf used to lead the mothers of the believers in the dawn prayer in Minya."
"13950","(13950) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Asbaaniyy. He said: Ibn Maqil told us, he said: Ka’b bin Ajra told me, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me, and it was And his head called him to prayer, and he said to me: Slay a sheep as a ritual, or fast for three days, or feed six poor people. Between every poor person is a saa' of dates. (Bukhari 1816, Muslim 85)"
"13951","(13951) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Mujahid; In the words of God Almighty: {So a ransom of fasting, or charity, or ritual sacrifice} They said: Fasting is three days, and charity is three days. Asa', and the rituals are performed."
"13952","(13952) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The ransom is fasting for ten days, and alms is fasting for ten days. Poor people, and the rituals are a sacrifice."
"13953","(13953) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Fasting for three days, and giving charity. Six poor people, and the rituals are a shame."
"13954","(13954) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Like him"
"13955","(13955) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, who said: Fasting is for three days. Alms are three times a share among six poor people, and rituals are a reward."
"13956","(13956) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr asked me and I told him, He said: This is what Ibn Abbas said."
"13957","(13957) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Sa’id bin Jubayr narrated to him, and he said: This is what he said. Ibn Abbas"
"13958","(13958) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: Fasting for three days. days, ritual rituals, and alms for six poor people."
"13959","(13959) Yahya bin Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Suddi, on the authority of Abu Malik; Like him"
"13960","(13960) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I heard him say regarding one who performs Hajj Then an illness afflicted him, or an injury to his head: he must fast for ten days, or feed ten poor people, or perform his rituals. What a shame"
"13961","(13961) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The one who adheres to what is between the pillar And the door."
"13962","(13962) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, who said: I saw Amr bin Maimun while he was standing between the pillar. And the door."
"13963","(13963) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: They used to adhere to what is between the pillar. And the door, and they pray."
"13964","(13964) Ruh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Adni, who said: I saw Ikrimah ibn Khalid, and his father Jafar, and Ikrimah, the servants of Ibn Abbas, stick to what is between the corner and the Kaaba’s door, and I saw them stick to what is below. The gutter in the stone."
"13965","(13965) Abu Yahya al-Razi Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hanzali, he said: I saw Salim, a peacock, and a peacock. They stick to what is between the corner and the door."
"13966","(13966) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Amr ibn Maymun sticking to his back. The Kaaba"
"13967","(13967) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz; He came to the back of the Kaaba seeking refuge."
"13968","(13968) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salih, who said: I saw Al-Qasim adhering to the side of the Kaaba."
"13969","(13969) Abu Yahya al-Razi told us, on the authority of Hanzali, he said: I saw al-Qasim seeking refuge in the back of the Kaaba, and he said: : Oh God, I seek refuge in You from Your wrath, Your vengeance, and Your authority."
"13970","(13970) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qays, who said: I saw Nafi’ bin Jubayr sticking to what is between the chapters. And the Hijr, and behind the Kaaba, both of which I have seen him do."
"13971","(13971) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah sticking behind The Ka'bah is from the night before Maghrib, and he clings to it to his chest."
"13972","(13972) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, who said: I saw Amr bin Maimun who had committed The Ka'bah, and cling to its stomach from its backside, from the side next to the Yemeni corner."
"13973","(13973) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad; That his father used to stick to the back of the Kaaba."
"13974","(13974) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I saw Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman committing a recent The Kaaba"
"13975","(13975) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who fasts for pleasure, then finds guidance before completing his fast. He said: He abandons fasting."
"13976","(13976) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning a man who fasted for three days during Hajj, then went away while he was in Mecca, it is due to him to give a sacrifice."
"13977","(13977) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, and Ikrimah; They said: If he is free before shaving, let him slaughter it."
"13978","(13978) Ibn Abi Rawad told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to say about the redemption of fasting: {or alms, or rituals}, about the ease of that, about Hajj and Umrah."
"13979","(13979) Ibn Abi Rawad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: If it is during Hajj, then until it is permissible And if it is during the Umrah, then until he circumambulates the Kaaba."
"13980","(13980) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muslim, on the authority of Ata’, Ibn Sirin, and al-Hasan. They said: If You fasted during the fulfillment of Hajj, then you find that before you have finished your fasting, then you are ungrateful, but if you find that you have finished your fasting, then it is not You must make atonement."
"13981","(13981) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Hatim bin Abi Saghira, on the authority of Ibn Abi Maliki, who said: I heard Ibn Al-Zubayr says: Seven hundred people of Israel used to perform Hajj to this house, and they would put their sandals in soft sand. And they will enter barefoot, out of respect for the House. (Fakihi 267)"
"13982","(13982) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: They hated to enter the house wearing shoes. And the sandal and the reed, as a glorification of the House."
"13983","(13983) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sharik, who said: I saw Ibn Umar walking around with his sandals on, And I saw Ibn al-Zubayr not doing it."
"13984","(13984) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I saw a peacock, a Mujahid, and a giant, roaming around... Their slippers"
"13985","(13985) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Mus’ab ibn Shayba, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr, he said: The mother was one of the sons of When Israel comes to Tuwa, they take off their sandals."
"13986","(13986) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: When the prophets came to the flag of the Sacred Mosque, they would remove Their slippers"
"13987","(13987) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kulayl, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: If You stoned the Jamarat, then everything is permissible for you except women, and he said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He covered his head with musk. Is that good or not? (Ahmad 1/369, Abu Ali 2688)"
"13988","(13988) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: If he stones the Jamarat and slaughters and shave, then everything is permissible for him except women."
"13989","(13989) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdullah bin Abi Al-Jahm, on the authority of Umar, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him (Abu Dawud 1972. Ahmad 6/143)"
"13990","(13990) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Al-Munkadir, he heard Ibn Al-Zubayr saying: If you stone the Jamarat from On the Day of Sacrifice, then what is after an-Nisaa has become lawful for you."
"13991","(13991) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: If he throws a stone, everything is permissible for him. Except women."
"13992","(13992) Jarir narrated to us, he said: Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If a person in ihram shave, everything is permissible for him except women. Until he circumambulates the Kaaba. If he circumambulates the Kaaba, women are permissible for him."
"13993","(13993) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: When he throws Everything is permissible for him at Jamarat, except for women."
"13994","(13994) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar, and Omar; They said: If a man slaughters and shave, everything is permissible for him except women and perfume."
"13995","(13995) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Nafi’ bin Umar, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he stones the Jamarat, everything is permissible for him, except for women."
"13996","(13996) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If he stones Jamarat Al-Aqba, everything is permissible for him, except perfume, women, and game."
"13997","(13997) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you have performed all of the rituals, then it is lawful for you. Everything, except women and game."
"13998","(13998) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Suleiman, who said: I kissed my wife after I stoned the Jamarat, so I asked Ataa? So he ordered me to slaughter a sheep."
"13999","(13999) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Al-Zubayr, he said: When he throws Jamarat is permissible for him for everything, except for women."
"14000","(14000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave a silver camel to Abu Jahl in his body. (Ibn Majah 31000, Ahmad 1/234)"
"14001","(14001) Ubayd Allah told us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah informed us, on the authority of Iyas bin Salamah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had a camel on his body. (Ibn Majah 3101)"
"14002","(14002) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked Ibn Umar: What do you see in his body? A sentence? He said: I have not seen anyone do that, and to slaughter a female is more beloved to me."
"14003","(14003) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Yahya Al-Ghasani, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah said: There is no harm in a male camel."
"14004","(14004) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: I have not seen anyone guide a camel except Omar bin Abdul Aziz, for he is the best guide."
"14005","(14005) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Females and males should be guided, and females are more beloved. To him"
"14006","(14006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, he said: Abu Ja’far, the client of Ibn Ayyash, told me, he said: I saw Ibn Ayash gave Mary two girls, one of which was circumcised."
"14007","(14007) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of a servant of Ibn Omar; That Ibn Umar gave a gift to two of his sisters."
"14008","(14008) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zam`a, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wahram, on the authority of Tawus, that he provided a camel for his enjoyment."
"14009","(14009) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Rabah ibn Abi Marouf, who said: It was said to Ata’: Ikrimah ibn Khalid He gave a camel. Ataa said: That is okay."
"14010","(14010) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was while the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, guided him. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him. (Tirmidhi 815. Abu Dawud 1746)"
"14011","(14011) Abd al-Rahman bin Muhammad al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He guided a camel."
"14012","(14012) Ismail Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I performed his Umrah in the month in which it is permissible."
"14013","(14013) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Muthanna, on the authority of Tawus, who said: I performed his Umrah in the month in which he entered the Sacred Mosque."
"14014","(14014) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of rain, on the authority of goodness, giving, and wisdom; They said: Whoever performs Umrah in one month, then circumambulates in another month, then I perform Umrah for him in the month in which he circumambulated."
"14015","(14015) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders; He said: His Umrah was in the month in which he entered ihram."
"14016","(14016) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I performed my Umrah in the month that falls. Therein"
"14017","(14017) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I performed his Umrah during the month in which he entered ihram."
"14018","(14018) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hisham told us, he said: Hafsa bint Sirin told us, she said: I came out Me and my brothers, so he rewarded us with life in Ramadan, so he offered us imprisonment until Shawwal came, so we asked the people of Mecca? So they all said to me: This is my pleasure."
"14019","(14019) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He said: I performed his Umrah in the month in which he entered ihram."
"14020","(14020) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He testifies to the sick person’s rituals. All of them, and he is circumambulated on a load. When he stones the Jamarat, it is placed in his palm, then he is thrown away with it from his palm."
"14021","(14021) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He throws stones from him."
"14022","(14022) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: The stone is thrown for the sick person, and tawaf is performed for him."
"14023","(14023) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ata’; They said: throw away it."
"14024","(14024) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abdul-Jabbar bin Ward, who said: My father sent me to Mujahid while he was sick, to ask him. About throwing stones? He said: He throws it on the behalf of his family."
"14025","(14025) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ata’; He said: The sick person should hire someone who will circumambulate for him."
"14026","(14026) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hanzala, who said: Tawus was asked about a sick woman? He said: Some of her family will throw her away."
"14027","(14027) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and with us were women and children, so we recited the prayers on behalf of the children and threw stones on their behalf. (Ahmad 3/314, Bayhaqi 156)"
"14028","(14028) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I saw a son of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, and I said: How? What do you do with this? They said: We put the pebble in his palm, and if he is unable to do so, he should throw it away."
